\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2016\par 17:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par U.K. TO CLOSE LOOPHOLE IN BANK BONUS CLAWBACKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bankers have previously been able to escape bonus clawbacks over rule breaking or excessive risk-taking by changing jobs. New proposals would empower new employers to impose penalties. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WHY BANKS SHOULD STOP STARS DODGING BONUS RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. regulators want to stop bonus buy-outs from undermining post-crisis rules on pay. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO MOVE HEAD OFFICE TO U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  probably won't be moving its headquarters to the U.S., but is likely to decide this year between staying in London or relocating to either Hong Kong or Paris, people familiar with the matter said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FED'S ROSENGREN: FUTURE RATE INCREASES LIKELY 'GRADUAL' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Boston President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eric Rosengren\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that it is best for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise short-term interest rates slowly as it faces ongoing risks from a troubled world economy and too-low inflation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMP TO CUT STAFF, SUSPEND DIVIDEND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GMP Capital plans to cut jobs, shutter its U.K. and Australian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and suspend its dividend as it tackles industry headwinds. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ECB POLICYMAKERS WORRIED BANKS ARE MOVING INTO RISKY AREAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's supervisory arm will look at whether banks in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc are adding risk to their business models to earn more in a low-interest rate environment, the vice-chair of the supervisory institution said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SWISS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  READY TO CURB FRANC GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss franc remains "considerably overvalued," with Switzerland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  willing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets if necessary, according to a top Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RUSSIA MULLS BUDGET CUTS AND BANK STAKE SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russian officials said Moscow may be forced to cut its budget by 10% and sell off stakes in the country's top lenders to offset a "long period" of low oil prices. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIA AIMS TO EASE FOREIGN-INVESTMENT RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia is working on a major revamp of foreign-investment rules that could open the door for overseas companies to take bigger stakes in domestic firms and gain a foothold in new industries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THE QUIET SIDE OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The 'national team,' a secretive group of state firms, has tried to shore up China's stock market on regulators' behalf, with mixed results. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KAZAKHSTAN FIRES WEALTH FUND MANAGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chief executive of Kazakhstan's National Investment Corp., which was set up to help manage the country's $64 billion oil fund, has been fired. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ABU DHABI WEALTH FUND APPOINTS PRIVATE-EQUITY CHIEF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Abu Dhabi's main sovereign-wealth fund has hired Sherwood Dodge, a former \f28 \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive, to spearhead its private-equity strategy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OFFSHORE YUAN BORROWING RATE COMES BACK TO EARTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong banks' cost of borrowing yuan from each other plunged Wednesday, one day after a liquidity squeeze sent the rate to stratospheric levels. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WHY CHINA'S HEFTY TRADE SURPLUS IS DWARFED BY OUTFLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It appears China suffered around $750 billion of capital outflow in 2015. No wonder the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is under pressure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 13, 2016 11:23 ET (16:23 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160113ec1d002f3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
