\par\par \b \uc2 China's War On Yuan Speculators Targets Wrong Problem -- Heard On The Street\b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2016\par 08:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par C12\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 1/13/16) \par    By Aaron Back \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [Financial Analysis and Commentary]\f28 \par \par \uc2 China has declared war on offshore speculators betting against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it is merely attacking a symptom, not the root causes, of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  woes.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the market for yuan traded offshore -- mostly in Hong Kong -- known by traders as CNH. Acting through state-owned banks, it has bought massive quantities of CNH, successfully closing the yawning gap that had opened between the yuan's value in Hong Kong and in mainland China.\par \par \uc2 This gap -- the CNH last week was trading at a discount of more than 2% -- was a source of embarrassment to the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 . It showed international markets were spooked, and didn't believe assurances there is "no basis" for continued yuan depreciation. Beijing essentially squeezed the market into dysfunction. The cost of borrowing CNH overnight in Hong Kong soared to almost 70% Tuesday, making it prohibitively expensive to keep betting against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This action comes at the cost of a long-term policy objective: to foster a vibrant offshore market for the yuan, eventually making it a widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  globally. By engineering a liquidity squeeze, China has introduced new risks into the offshore market that will make it less attractive to investors. As always, maintaining control is Beijing's priority; other goals come second.\par \par \uc2 Asserting control over the CNH market is simple. Total CNH deposits in Hong Kong in November were 864 billion yuan, or $132 billion at current exchange rates. That is easily overwhelmed by China's $3.33 trillion of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The bigger problem is the flow of money out of mainland \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been costly; \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves fell by half a trillion dollars in 2015. In December alone, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely spent $130 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  estimates. This has the nasty side effect of shrinking the domestic money supply, adding to deflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 Closing the gap between onshore and offshore yuan is meant to reverse investor expectations for continued yuan depreciation. But the outflows pushing the yuan lower have fundamental drivers. Growth is slowing and interest rates are falling, driving down investment returns. So money is naturally leaving China and seeking better returns elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Since China can disrupt the yuan anytime, shorting it could be hazardous in the near term. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-term direction is still to the downside. That in turn should drive down \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of commodity exporters such as Australia, a more straightforward bet.\par \par \uc2 China can muscle the small CNH market into submission. But until it convinces its own people to stop taking money out of the country, the appearance of control will be illusory.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 13, 2016 02:34 ET (07:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160113ec1d000j3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
