\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Oil drama keeps stocks subdued, yuan rates converge\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marc Jones   \par \uc2 989 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Emerging market stocks fell again on Tuesday to take their losses since the start of the year to almost 7 percent, and there was more drama in Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets as authorities in Beijing grappled to exert control.\par \par \uc2 Chinese shares had a quiet day by recent standards but a drop by oil towards $30 a barrel sent Saudi Arabian, Russian and other oil dependent markets sliding again and left \uc2 MSCI\uc2 's 26-country EM index at a new 6-1/2 year low.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Saudi, the world's biggest oil producer, fell as much as 2.6 percent, extending their losses since the start of 2016 to over 13 percent and 'forwards' showed pressure on the 'pegged' riyal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at record levels.\par \par \uc2 Dollar denominated Russian stocks hit their lowest in over a year before a bounce in oil eased the pressure, while Turkey's lira hit its lowest in over three months after an explosion in central Istanbul killed at least several people.\par \par \uc2 Things were by no means quiet in China, either, despite the relative calm in equity markets.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC)\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had been aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 'offshore' yuan markets to prop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up after it had also nudged the 'official' rate higher in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 But that in turn sucked much of the yuan liquidity out of the system to such an extent that overnight yuan borrowing rates in Hong Kong (HIBOR) hit a record high, and the spread between onshore and offshore yuan exchange rates briefly evaporated.\par \par \uc2 "This is not a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war. China is allowing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to free float and the market is telling us it believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is too strong," said Simon Quijano-Evans, chief EM strategist, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That means there will be capital outflows and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will weaken to find its new equilibrium. That's the stage we're in," he added, predicting further falls in the yuan this year.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker amid the ongoing China uncertainty. Malaysia's ringgit was still feeling the effects of a \uc2 Moody's\uc2  sovereign outlook cut as well as the latest drop in oil, one of its big revenue earners.\par \par \uc2 Commodity-dependent Kazakhstan's tenge was on the end of another hiding though there was a 1 percent bounce to $16.25 for South Africa's rand after it had fallen almost 10 percent at one point on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Central and eastern Europe saw its first Eurobond issuance of 2016, with Poland selling a 10-and 20-year dual-tranche offer.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps reflecting concerns about the direction being taken by the country's new government, the deal did not appear to inspire investors with demand lacklustre. Analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said it was "not a good sign for the region."\par \par \uc2 Polish stocks though were on a tear, up over 2.5 percent as broader European stocks began to rebound from the China-led slump.\par \par \uc2 There was also parliamentary hearings for the first wave of new candidates in what will be a complete revamp of the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policymaking council in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "Given that the new government has indicated they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to actively support economic activity, the new council is expected to be a lot more dovish than the outgoing one," said Piotr Matys an economist at Rabobank.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus35t}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  emerging index performance, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  emerging Europe performance, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  frontier index performance, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see )\par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging Markets Prices from Reuters            \par  Equities                  Latest    Net Chg  % Chg  % Chg\par               \par               \par on year\par               \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2                \par  Emrg Mkt Indx    722.58    -0.78   -0.11   -9.01\par               \par Czech Rep            917.33    -1.31   -0.14   -4.08\par               \par Poland           1751.54   +47.76   +2.80   -5.79\par               \par Hungary           24024.79  +124.11   +0.52   +0.44\par               \par Romania           6548.60   -59.81   -0.91   -6.51\par               \par Greece              584.50    +2.82   +0.48   -7.42\par               \par Russia             