   \par Sov'gn Debt  EMBIG   467        -3    .06  6 66.62 \par  All data taken from Reuters \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily U.S.    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Claire Milhench) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-12T11:38:07.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160112ec1c00e1y\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 French Market Climbs, But EDF Falls\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2016 NoticiasFinancieras. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (RTTNews) - The French market was firmly in positive territory on Tuesday, despite weak cues from Asia. Sentiment improved after China's offshore yuan firmed above the onshore rate for the first time since October, spurred by what traders called aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Beijing.\par \par \uc2 Ma Jun, the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief economist, said that \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to keep the yuan basically stable against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and fluctuations of the yuan against the dollar will increase.\par \par \uc2 In economic news, the French economy is forecast to expand 0.3 percent in the fourth quarter, unrevised from the previous estimate, \uc2 the Bank of France\uc2  said. The business confidence index rose slightly to 99 in December, while it was forecast to remain unchanged at 98.\par \par \uc2 U.K. industrial production declined unexpectedly in November on falling energy output, figures from the \uc2 Office for National Statistics\uc2  showed. Industrial output slid 0.7 percent month-on-month after staying flat in October. It was forecast to grow 0.1 percent in November.\par \par \uc2 The Euro Stoxx 50 index of eurozone bluechip stocks advanced 1.58 percent, while the Stoxx Europe 50 index, which includes some major U.K. companies, rose 1.16 percent.\par \par \uc2 The CAC 40 index gained 2.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Telecom firm Orange jumped 4 percent. Luxury goods firm \uc2 LVMH\uc2  and electrical products maker Legrand added 3.6 percent and 2.6 percent, in that order.\par \par \uc2 Auto parts maker \uc2 Valeo\uc2  added 3.5 percent. Renault rose 3.4 percent and \uc2 Peugeot\uc2  surged 6.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Lenders BNP Paribas, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  and \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  were firmly in positive territory.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bucking the trend, EDF declined around 5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Other markets in the region also advanced on the day.\par \par \uc2 Most Asian shares fell in cautious trading, as oil took another tumble and Chinese stocks seesawed before the release of trade data on Wednesday, which is expected to show further declines in both exports and imports.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., futures point to a higher open on Wall Street. Stocks ended Monday's session narrowly mixed as a slump in crude oil prices weighed on energy stocks, offsetting gains in consumer and technology stocks.\par \par \uc2 Crude for February delivery fell $0.70 to $30.71 per barrel, while February gold slipped $0.1 to $1096.1 a troy ounce.\par \par \uc2 For comments and feedback: contact editorial@rttnews.com\par \par \uc2 Copyright(c) 2016 RTTNews.com. All Rights Reserved\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020160112ec1c003h4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
