\par\par \b \uc2 Onshore and offshore yuan converge, offshore liquidity tightens\b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par 05:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Jan 12 (Reuters) - China's offshore yuan was\par trading almost in line with its onshore counterpart on Tuesday,\par with the offshore yuan implied overnight deposit rate hitting a\par record high, indicating extremely tight liquidity outside the\par mainland.\par     China's offshore yuan implied overnight deposit rate\par  hit a record high of 94 percent in Hong Kong on\par Tuesday, with analysts saying the spike was caused by the\par Peoples' Bank of China (\f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) buying yuan offshore to support\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which drained liquidity. \par     Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates for offshore yuan (CNH\par HIBOR) also hit record highs on Monday, as a combination of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and arbitrage drained\par offshore yuan supply. \par     "The market suspects that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is possibly using major\par state banks to directly drain yuan liquidity in offshore\par markets," said a dealer at an European bank in Shanghai.  \par     The dealer described the strength of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par actions as being of "nuclear-weapon" level strength. \par     "Its actions are comparable to steps taken by other central\par banks when they previously fought against international\par speculators, such as George Soros," he said.\par     Prior to market open, The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.5628 per dollar, almost unchanged from the\par previous fix 6.5626. \par     The spot market opened at 6.5770 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.5717 at midday, only 0.03 percent weaker\par than the previous close. \par     The offshore yuan was trading 68 pips, or 0.1\par percent softer than the onshore spot at 6.5785 per dollar. \par     The spread between onshore and offshore yuan hit its widest\par level in more than four years to more than 1,200 pips a week\par before, offering investors the opportunity to arbitrage the rate\par difference by paying off onshore debt with offshore yuan.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which will include the yuan\par in its reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket, reportedly mentioned the wide\par spread between onshore and offshore yuan levels at the weekend\par and was said to have discussions with Chinese officials on the\par subject.\par     That has strengthened market expectation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will conduct more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "There is still a lot of swaps squeezing going on. The\par funding for the swap positions is being squeezed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via Chinese banks that used to be main\par liquidity providers of the offshore yuan," said the head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par trading at an Asian bank in Hong Kong.   \par     "It will last for a few days and perhaps we'll see some\par relief later this week as a lot of short yuan positions will be\par forced to be squared within days."\par     Still, some traders said that market's expectation of yuan's\par depreciation remained unchanged, given that the spread between\par forward rates in onshore and offshore market are still wide.\par     The onshore one-year forwards contract was\par trading at 6.6898, while the offshore one-year forwards contract\par  was trading at a discount of 3.31 percent at 6.9115.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.5628   6.5626    0.00%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.5717   6.5695    -0.03%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.14%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -5.60%\par  Spot change since 2005                25.94%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.5785    -0.10%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.918     -5.13%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom and Lu Jianxin; Additional\par Reporting by Michelle Chen in Hong Kong; Editing by Sam Holmes)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-12T05:22:08.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160112ec1c0060p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw