\par\par \b \uc2 European Morning Briefing: Stocks Set for Tentative Gains Despite China Uncertainty\b0\par\par\uc2 3,132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par 05:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Snapshot: \par ======== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks set for modest rebound; EUR/USD 1.0861, yuan steady; bonds seen flat; Brent crude at $31.23; gold at $1096.00\f28 \par \par \uc2 -Oil Skids to 12-Year Low\par \par \uc2 -China State Planner Predicts 2015 Economic Growth of About 7%\par \par \uc2 -Offshore Yuan Overnight Interbank Borrowing Rate Hits Record High of 66.815%\par \par \uc2 -Fed's Kaplan: Continuing Path of Monetary Policy Normalization Important\par \par \uc2 -Fed's Lockhart Expects Economy to Justify Further Rate Increases in 2016\par \par \uc2 -SAP Reports 3% Drop in Operating Profit, Offers Optimistic Guidance\par \par \uc2 -Alcoa Reports 18% Drop in Revenue\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 UniCredit\uc2  to Sell Ukrainian Unit to \uc2 Alfa Group\par \par \uc2 Watch For: Eurozone 2Q economic outlook; U.K. industrial production, manufacturing output \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Headline News: \par ============= \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic planner said Tuesday that the nation's economic growth in 2015 is expected to be about 7%, on par with the government's target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Annual growth of 7% would be the weakest performance in a quarter century. China's statistics bureau is set to release the data Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Robert Kaplan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas, said it is important for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue gradually raising short-term interest rates given potential distortions to the economy if rates are too low for too long.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "[I]f we delay further normalization until we actually see evidence of excessive accommodation, there is a risk that we will have waited too long," Mr. Kaplan said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. economy likely will withstand financial-market volatility if it doesn't last too long, allowing more interest-rate increases this year, Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dennis Lockhart\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I expect further rate increases will be justified by economic performance in 2016," Mr. Lockhart said, adding that rate rises can't be firmly predicted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is no predetermined schedule of increases, no preset path of policy. No map. Monetary policy is not on autopilot," Mr. Lockhart said, adding that the performance of inflation data will be key to what actions central bankers take. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Stocks: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks should open in positive territory following a rebound in the U.S. on Monday and despite a mixed performance in Asia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ahead of Tuesday's open, IG has called the DAX up 77 points, the CAC up 31 and the FTSE up 29.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in Asia steadied Tuesday, though trading remained choppy in China.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Shanghai Composite Index rose 0.4% to 3028.04, but it traded up and down as much as 1% from its previous close. Elsewhere, the S&P/ASX 200 fell 0.1% and Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index rose 0.2%. In Japan, where markets were closed for national holiday Monday, the Nikkei Stock Average tracked Monday's regional losses, falling 2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow industrials rallied in the final hour of trading Monday, closing in positive territory and capping a day of wide swings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 52 points to 16399, after swinging between gains and losses throughout the session and falling as much as 114 points in intraday trade. Many investors are bracing for higher levels of volatility in stocks in the weeks ahead, holding off on placing big trades ahead of fourth-quarter earnings reports from many U.S. companies, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The S&P 500 rose less than 0.1%, while the Nasdaq Composite declined 0.1%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Corporate News: \par ============== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German business software provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAP\f28 \uc2 \f2  late Monday pre-announced some figures for the fourth quarter and fiscal year 2015, reporting a 3% drop in operating profit for the fourth quarter of 2015, even as it laid out an optimistic guidance for 2016.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fourth-quarter operating profit for the period ended Dec. 31 was EUR1.7 billion, compared with EUR1.75 billion during the same period last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAP\f28 \uc2 \f2  also provided a fourth-quarter operating profit figure of EUR2.28 billion, based on calculations that aren't recognized under international financial reporting standards. That figure was a 3% increase year-over-year and in line with analysts' forecasts, according to a recent poll conducted by The Wall Street Journal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that it reached an agreement to sell its Ukrainian unit, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ukrsotsbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ABH Holdings, in a transaction likely to cost the bank about EUR852 million ($930.8 million).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Italian bank said the deal reached will lead to a charge of roughly EUR200 million the bank will book in its earnings for the fourth quarter of last year, as a net result of the sale.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alcoa\f28 \uc2 \f2  said its fourth-quarter revenue slumped 18% amid sharply lower aluminum prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares rose 2.1% to $8.17 in after-hours trading as adjusted per-share earnings, which exclude restructuring costs and other one-time items, beat expectations. Through the close of the regular session, the stock had fallen 50% over the past year. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan continued to stabilize Tuesday, though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  guided the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slightly weaker.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier, Chinese authorities fixed the yuan at 6.5628 per U.S. dollar compared with 6.5626 Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's onshore yuan, which can trade 2% above or below the fix, last traded at 6.5733 per dollar, weaker than 6.5695 at Monday's close. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reached a five-year low of 6.5956 last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit its strongest level since the beginning of the year on Tuesday, and last traded at 6.5705.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders say the offshore yuan has been strengthening as state-owned Chinese banks buy the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a sign of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . That has limited the supply of the offshore yuan, tightening liquidity and sending the rate at which Hong Kong banks lend yuan to each other overnight to a record high of 66.815% on Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A lot of channels bringing money from onshore to offshore market have been blocked, which also contributes to the shortage of yuan in Hong Kong," said Tommy Ong, head of Wealth Management Solutions at DBS in Hong Kong.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The daily EUR/USD chart is currently inconclusive, while the pair remains stuck inside the Ichimoku Cloud consolidation zone that spans 1.0790-1.1017, and also within a no-man's land demarcated by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unless EUR/USD manages to end Tuesday out of the 1.0828-1.0951 range suggested by the Bollinger bands, in so doing triggering the Bollinger downtrend or uptrend channels, technical consolidation is likely to persist.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The gains for U.S. stocks, and the possibility of a further recovery of China's yuan could help general risk-taking appetite to improve, which would be bearish for EUR/USD because the euro behaves like a funding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0042 GMT, EUR/USD was 1.0861 from its Monday close of 1.0859. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Bonds: \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European bond prices will start little changed as investors make tentative moves back into equities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices of short-term \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt strengthened Monday, sending the two-year note's yield to a one-month low, as the 5.3% selloff in crude oil boosted demand for haven assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Long-term bonds pulled back ahead of fresh new debt sales.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors say the uncertain global outlook would push the Fed to be slow in raising interest rates to avoid undermining the growth momentum in the U.S., which would keep lid on bond yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Global growth concerns are weighing on expectations for the pace of Fed's interest rate increases this year which is benefiting" short-term Treasury debt, said Larry Milstein, head of government and agency trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 R.W. Pressprich & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the two-year note, highly sensitive to changes in the Fed's rate policy outlook, was 0.928% by late afternoon in New York, compared with 0.948% Friday. The yield on the benchmark 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  note was 2.160%, compared with a two-month low of 2.131% Friday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Energy: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil prices fell harder in Asia on Tuesday as traders built up short positions in the midst of crumbling confidence in the Chinese economy and a growing global glut.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 , light, sweet crude futures for delivery in February traded at $31.09 a barrel at 0343 GMT, down $0.32 in the Globex electronic session. February Brent crude on London's \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures exchange fell $0.32 to $31.23 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil prices plunged more than 5% on Monday to trade near $30 a barrel, making the specter of bankruptcy ever more likely for a significant chunk of the U.S. oil industry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  now expect the price of oil to crash through the $30 threshold and into $20 territory in short order as a result of China's slowdown, the U.S. dollar's appreciation and the fact that drillers from Houston to Riyadh won't quit pumping despite the oil glut.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As many as a third of American oil-and-gas producers could tip toward bankruptcy and restructuring by mid-2017, according to Wolfe Research. Survival, for some, would be possible if oil rebounded to at least $50, according to analysts. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Metals: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices were a touch higher in Asia, even though they remained below a psychological level of $1,100/ounce.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The robust U.S. dollar also weighed on gold, said ANZ but if the turbulence in China's stock market continues, gold prices are likely to gain, analysts said. At 0232 GMT, spot gold was at $1,096.00, marginally higher than the previous close at $1,094.10.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to paul.larkins@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11 Jan 2016 23:41 ET \par European Morning Briefing: DJ Exclusive Headlines; Other Top Stories\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DJ Exclusive Headlines:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apollo Global Management\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Talks to Buy Apollo Education\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/apollo-education-to-explore-strategic-alternatives-1452516388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/apollo-education-to-explore-strategic-alternatives-1452516388}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Norway's Voss Says China's Reignwood To Buy Majority Stake\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/norways-voss-says-chinas-reignwood-to-buy-majority-stake-1452546071"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/norways-voss-says-chinas-reignwood-to-buy-majority-stake-1452546071}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya Plans Oil Loading at Eastern Port for First Time Since 2014\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/libya-plans-oil-loading-at-eastern-port-for-first-time-since-2014-1452532497"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/libya-plans-oil-loading-at-eastern-port-for-first-time-since-2014-1452532497}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Amazon to Release Portable Version of Echo Speaker in Coming Weeks\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/amazon-to-release-portable-version-of-echo-speaker-in-coming-weeks-1452532671"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/amazon-to-release-portable-version-of-echo-speaker-in-coming-weeks-1452532671}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Top Stories:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil Skids to 12-Year Low\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil took another tumble, with the U.S. benchmark price dropping to its lowest level since December 2003.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/oil-prices-tumble-weighed-by-china-worries-1452481849"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/oil-prices-tumble-weighed-by-china-worries-1452481849}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 China State Planner Predicts 2015 Economic Growth of About 7%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic planner said Tuesday that the nation's economic growth in 2015 is expected to be about 7%, on par with the government's target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Offshore Yuan Overnight Interbank Borrowing Rate Hits Record High of 66.815%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The liquidity in the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong continued to dry up Tuesday as the overnight interbank borrowing rate soared to a record high of 66.815%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed's Kaplan: Continuing Path of Monetary Policy Normalization Important\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Robert Kaplan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas, said it is important for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue gradually raising short-term interest rates given potential distortions to the economy if rates are too low for too long.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed's Lockhart Expects Economy to Justify Further Rate Increases in 2016\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. economy likely will withstand financial-market volatility if it doesn't last too long, allowing more interest-rate increases this year, Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dennis Lockhart\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iran Nuclear Deal to Fully Take Effect Soon, Says \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Mogherini\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Iranian nuclear deal and the lifting of most economic and financial sanctions on Tehran will take effect soon but there is no fixed date yet, European Union foreign-policy chief Federica Mogherini said on Monday.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/iran-nuclear-deal-to-fully-take-effect-soon-says-eus-mogherini-1452536725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/iran-nuclear-deal-to-fully-take-effect-soon-says-eus-mogherini-1452536725}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Current Account Surplus More Than Doubles in November\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus expanded in November due to strong income from overseas investments and as the goods and services deficit narrowed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish Bank BBVA Hires Barclays Top Tech Executive\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  hired Derek White, one of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's top digital executives, as the Spanish bank continues to ramp up its investment in new technology.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/spanish-bank-bbva-hires-barclays-top-tech-executive-1452541070"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/spanish-bank-bbva-hires-barclays-top-tech-executive-1452541070}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 SAP Reports 3% Drop in Operating Profit, Offers Optimistic Guidance\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German business software provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAP SE\f28 \uc2 \f2  late Monday pre-announced some figures for the fourth quarter and fiscal year 2015, reporting a 3% drop in operating profit for the fourth quarter of 2015, even as it laid out an optimistic guidance for 2016.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/sap-reports-3-drop-in-operating-profit-offers-optimistic-guidance-1452557975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/sap-reports-3-drop-in-operating-profit-offers-optimistic-guidance-1452557975}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Alcoa Swings to a Loss on Charges\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alcoa Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . swung to a loss in its fourth quarter on restructuring charges and its revenue fell 18% compare with a year ago amid sharply lower aluminum prices.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/alcoa-reports-18-drop-in-revenue-1452546975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/alcoa-reports-18-drop-in-revenue-1452546975}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 11 Jan 2016 23:41 ET \par European Morn