\par\par \b \uc2 In  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's Balancing Act, More 'Reluctant  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2 ' -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par 03:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0213 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Chinese securities regulators are playing a challenging balancing act. They want to control market turmoil to calm panic selling while trying to make good on its pledges to the world that market forces, rather than the government, are guiding capital investment. Given the tumult last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have no choice but to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now to buy shares and prevent excessive volatility, \uc2 Eurasia Group\uc2  analysts say in a note. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will "continue its reluctant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive volatility and remain an active purchaser of shares," they say. But there will be an end to Beijing's grip on the market, they write. At some point China will have to "allow it [the market] to operate more freely, which is a key goal for this leadership team and one identified explicitly in a range of reform documents over the past few years." The Hang Seng Index opens up 0.5% against the Shanghai Composite Index's 0.1% gain Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2  (dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0157 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The yuan slipped slightly against the U.S. dollar in the onshore spot market, despite the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  marking the daily USD/CNY benchmark nearly unchanged at 6.5628 versus Monday's 6.5626. Recent yuan weakness, which has fuelled speculative bets on even sharper yuan-depreciation this year, has prompted authorities to downplay the possibility that yuan is in a tailspin lower. "Attempts to sell short the renminbi will not succeed" says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Han Jun\f28 \uc2 \f2 , deputy director of the office of the Central Leading Group on Financial and Economic Affairs. Onshore USD/CNY is now 6.5733 from its Monday close of 6.5695 representing a marginally weaker yuan, while the offshore yuan is at 6.6046 from 6.5833 representing a 0.3% weakening versus the dollar. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0145 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's stock market tumble last week is not a reflection of changes in the real economy, rather it has more to do with design flaws of the circuit breakers, said Nobel prize-winning economist Joseph Stiglitz. The circuit breaker was designed to halt trading for 15 minutes after a 5% swing and for the rest of the trading day if the move reached 7%. The two levels were too close to each other and compelled investors to rush to get out before next level was reached, said Stiglitz, adding that circuit breakers remain necessary for market stability and must be correctly designed. The Shanghai and Shenzhen stock markets lost as much as 7.4 trillion yuan ($1.1 trillion) Monday through Thursday last week and twice shut early after the circuit breaker was triggered. The mechanism was suspended late Thursday. (esther.fung@wsj.com, @estherfung) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0144 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] In a sign that Indonesia is getting friendlier to foreign workers, the government will issue permits for hiring expatriate workers in new investment projects in just three hours. This if investors commit to investing at least 100 billion rupiah or employ at least 1,000 local workers. Vice President Jusuf Kalla said Indonesia must not consider foreign workers coming to the country as competitors to local people, but as part of job creation. The Manpower Ministry last year planned to introduce a raft of regulations to make it difficult for hiring expatriate workers, but President Joko Widodo ordered the ministry to cancel such plans following an outcry from foreign companies. His government is also striving to attract foreign direct investment to revive economic growth (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0139 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japanese stocks are lower, dragged down by energy-related firms, amid instability in global markets, particularly crude oil. Oil explorer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inpex Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (1605.TO) is down 4.2% at 1,053.0 yen. Oil distributor \f28 \uc2 \f2 JX Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (5020.TO) is down 4.3% at Y447.9. Still, some analysts say bearish bets against stocks have been building up, and that stock selling could soon be easing on the back of a recovery in the Chinese yuan, a source of the recent market instability. "We don't know what would be a trigger, but short-covering could kick in (given the sizable accumulation of negative positions)," says Mitsushige Akino, chief fund manager at Ichiyoshi Investment Management. The Nikkei is down 1.3% at 17464.86.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0134 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Tuesday's USD/CNY daily benchmark of 6.5628 versus yesterday's 6.5626 represents a virtually unchanged yuan versus the U.S. dollar. The stability of the daily USD/CNY parity rate is slightly surprising given that the offshore yuan posted a sharp 1.5% gain versus the dollar on Monday. The movement of the offshore yuan, which typically represents market forces more accurately than the onshore yuan due to availability of liquidity and fewer trading constraints, is a factor in determining the daily onshore USD/CNY benchmark rate. Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have so far barely reacted to the yuan benchmark's miniscule gain versus the U.S. dollar, awaiting the opening of the spot yuan market. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0123 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Hong Kong stocks Tuesday will be heavily influenced by how \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and battered stock markets. Traders are looking for any chance to buy oversold equities, including signals from China to implement more market-supporting policies. Hang Seng Index futures are up 0.5%. "If we see heavy state \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the mainland equity markets alongside these new moves to prop up the CNY, then this could be the jump start needed to see a bit of buying come back into global equities" at least in the short term, brokerage IG says in a note. Expectations of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were driven by an overnight statement from Ma Jun, the chief economist at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 . He said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to create a new system to "appropriately limit" daily yuan-versus-U.S. dollar volatility. (dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0117 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Shares of Sharp (6753.TO) are up 1.8% to 116 yen following reports of a possible bailout by a government-led fund and Sharp's main lenders. The Nikkei reported that, under a proposal made by the government-led Innovation Network of Japan, Sharp would receive an investment of some 200 billion yen ($1.68 billion). Also, 150 billion yen of the loans from the two main lenders would be transferred to a new liquid crystal display entity and converted to preferred shares. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0112 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The search for growth in the Australian economy is set to remain a nagging problem for policymakers in 2016, says Pimco. The dominant question going forward will continue to be what will fill the hole left by the mining sector? That question is set to get even more urgent as stimulus to the economy from a housing construction booms fades, Pimco adds in a research note. "This is not to say we envision a significant housing correction, but we certainly expect the housing market tailwind to subside," it said. The less than spectacular growth environment in Australian will leave open the question of whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will need to cut interest rates further from their current record low of 2.0%. (james.glynn@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1106 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] After being triggered twice on two trading days, China's circuit breaker rules were scrapped by regulators the same week they were introduced. The rules halted trading for 15 minutes if the CSI 300 fell by 5% and for the full day if the index dropped by 7%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says China's circuit-breaker rules--versions of which are commonly seen in other markets around the world--failed for three reasons. First, they shut down liquidity. Second, the circuit breaker prevented brokerages from selling shares pledged against loans, should a client fail to meet a margin call. Finally, the circuit breaker led to collapsed brokerage commissions--on Jan. 7, China share turnover shrank to 188 billion yuan ($28.6 billion) (compared with a daily average of 1.05 trillion yuan for 2015)--because trading was halted. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  didn't say, but might have added, that the rules were designed to curtail volatility but had done anything but. (jasper.moiseiwitsch@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @moiseiwitsch) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KBC \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0050 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely keep its policy rate on hold at the current record-low 1.5% for a seventh consecutive month when its policy board meets later this week. The latest Wall Street Journal poll shows 19 of 20 analysts surveyed expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  to stand pat on the benchmark seven-day repurchase rate at its Jan. 14 meeting. Only one analyst expects a quarter-percentage-point rate cut at the upcoming meeting. The BOK may want to "take more time to assess the growing drag from China's weakening appetite for its [Korea's] exports" before probably easing further in February or March to help spur anemic growth, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in a note. Recent BOK minutes hint that the bank may trim its growth forecast of 3.2% for 2016 in a new outlook on Jan. 14. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11 Jan 2016 21:13 ET \par In China's Balancing Act, More 'Reluctant -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0042 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The daily EUR/USD chart is currently inconclusive, while the pair remains stuck inside the Ichimoku Cloud consolidation zone that spans 1.0790-1.1017, and also within a no-man's land demarcated by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1). Unless EUR/USD manages to end Tuesday out of the 1.0828-1.0951 range suggested by the Bollinger bands, in so doing triggering the Bollinger downtrend or uptrend channels, technical consolidation is likely to persist. The overnight rise of U.S. stocks, and the possibility of a further recovery of China's yuan - based on Monday's sharp gain for the offshore yuan, which is a factor in determining the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate onshore - could help general risk-taking appetite to improve, which would be bearish for the EUR/USD pair because the euro behaves like a funding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . EUR/USD is now 1.0861 from its Monday close of 1.0859. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 11, 2016 21:13 ET (02:13 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160112ec1c0007l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
