\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-UPDATE 1-HK offshore yuan interbank rates hit record highs on \uc2 PBOC \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2016\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects quotation in paragraph 7, clarifies title)\par \par \uc2 By Pete Sweeney and Saikat Chatterjee\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/HONG KONG, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates for offshore yuan (CNH HIBOR) all hit record highs on Monday, as a combination of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and arbitrage drained offshore yuan supply.\par \par \uc2 The overnight rate spiked to over 13 percent on Monday, up from 4 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Other offshore CNH tenors stood at similar record highs, ranging from 11 percent for the one-week CNH HIBOR to 5.2 percent for the one-year tenor.\par \par \uc2 All are much higher than the onshore rates quoted in Shanghai (SHIBOR), where the overnight rate, while up from previously, is still below 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying up offshore yuan and selling dollars in order to support the weakening offshore yuan was draining liquidity and behind the spike.\par \par \uc2 Companies rushing to borrow offshore yuan, which is cheaper than onshore, to repay onshore debts was also contributing to the spike, another trader said.\par \par \uc2 "The policy from \uc2 PBOC\uc2  last November has kept offshore liquidity tight, because it limits transfers from onshore to offshore," said James Lee, a rates strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in Singapore, speaking generally about recent conditions in the offshore market.\par \par \uc2 The onshore yuan has slid over 6 percent since August, sparking investor fears that Beijing is preparing for a far deeper devaluation in the yuan.\par \par \uc2 That has caused markets to price the offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a deep discount to the onshore version, as wide as 2 percent on some days, offering investors the opportunity to arbitrage the rate diffference by paying off onshore debt with offshore yuan.\par \par \uc2 The offshore yuan was trading 1.2 percent weaker than the onshore spot in early afternoon, at 6.6641 per dollar compared to 6.5832 onshore.\par \par \uc2 Yuan accumulation in the offshore market lost momentum in 2015 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest yearly loss on record against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Yuan deposits in Hong Kong stood at 864.2 billion yuan ($131.35 billion) in November, a bit higher than 854.3 billion yuan a month earlier but still hovering around two-year lows.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , which will include the yuan in its reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket starting in October, reportedly mentioned the wide spread between onshore and offshore yuan levels at the weekend and was said to have discussions with Chinese officials on the subject. That has strengthened market expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will conduct more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom and Michelle Chen in HONG KONG; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-11T12:19:26.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160111ec1b0086o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
