\par\par \b \uc2 Offshore Yuan Liquidity Tightens in Hong Kong\b0\par\par\uc2 By Fiona Law   \par \uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2016\par 08:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--The liquidity for the offshore yuan in Hong Kong, the main trading hub of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outside the mainland, sharply tightened amid Chinese banks' efforts last week to ramp up the yuan.\par \par \uc2 The short-term borrowing rates Hong Kong banks charge each other for yuan borrowing surged to a record high Monday. The overnight rate jumped to 13.4% from 4% Friday, while the rate to borrow the yuan for a week soared to 11.23% from 7.05%--both are levels unseen since the inception of the benchmark rate in 2013.\par \par \uc2 The offshore fixing rate is a benchmark based on reference rates contributed by local banks and compiled by the Treasury Markets Association, the city's banking industry group.\par \par \uc2 Traders attributed the liquidity squeeze to the efforts of Chinese banks, proxies for \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last week to support the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "As these banks are holding the yuan instead of releasing it to the market," the pool of yuan funds offshore shrinks and liquidity dries up, said a senior trader at a major local bank.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese banks were seen buying up the yuan aggressively late last week after a sharp fall in the offshore Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  left it trading at a deep discount to its mainland counterpart, roiling global markets from stocks to commodities.\par \par \uc2 Unlike the tightly controlled yuan in the onshore market, the offshore yuan is freely traded and reflects international investors' sentiment toward China's economic health and the outlook for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The increase in the offshore yuan rates effectively makes it painfully expensive for speculators, who typically borrow, to short the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Because of this, as well the shakeup stemming from the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, trading in the offshore yuan market has become quieter. The value of the offshore yuan, or CNH, has stabilized to 6.6660 a dollar mid-afternoon Asia on Monday, as compared with 6.6820 a dollar late Friday.\par \par \uc2 Another reason for the tightened offshore yuan liquidity was the narrowing of pipes for yuan funds to cross the border from onshore to offshore amid authorities' effort to stem capital outflows, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Recently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has suspended some foreign banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  businesses in China to make it harder for foreign investors to bet against the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "These funds used to be a constant supply of yuan cash in the offshore market," said Tommy Ong, head of Wealth Management Solutions at \uc2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\uc2 . in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Write to Fiona Law at fiona.law@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 11, 2016 02:16 ET (07:16 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160111ec1b000h8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
