\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong Stocks--Financials, Property, Oil--Slide -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2016\par 05:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0439 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Hang Seng Index slides 2.5% to 19,953 midday Monday, hit by losses in financials, property and oil stocks. The Hong Kong dollar weakened to a 10-month low in its trading band against the U.S. dollar, causing some traders to suspect investors are pulling money out of Hong Kong. Financials stocks have been selling off heavily. "Market conditions will remain challenging in the short to medium term, given weak growth and volatility in external markets, [and] renminbi depreciation pressure," writes \uc2 William Wong\uc2 , head of institutional sales trading at Shenwan Hongyuan Securities. Chinese property stocks fell, led by \uc2 China Resources Land\uc2  (1109.HK) down 5.8%, while weak oil prices dragged oil stocks lower, with \uc2 PetroChina\uc2  (0857.HK) down 4.9%. Chinese retailer Chow Tai Fook (1929.HK) also fell 4.5% after reporting lower-than-expected quarterly sales. (dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] South Korea's incoming Finance Minister Yoo Il-ho hints he is seeking a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deal with Japan after the Asian neighbors ended their old arrangement last year amid chilly relations. "It is worth thinking about reviving a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deal with Japan and expanding other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps" to bolster Seoul's buffer against possible capital flight in the wake of U.S. interest rate increases, Yoo says during a parliament hearing in Seoul Monday. His remarks--in response to a lawmaker asking about a need for the deal--but disclosed no further details. A previous Korean-Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap was once worth as much as $70 billion at its peak, but it shrank to $10 billion when it was terminated on February 23 last year, when the two countries stumbled through a diplomatic row over Japan's 1910-1945 colonial rule of Koreans. Recently, there are some signs of bilateral ties thawing with an accord last month to end the decades-old dispute over Korean women used as sex slaves by Japan during World War II. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0434 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India shares have opened lower on worries over China. Though analysts have repeatedly said India is more resilient to external shocks, either from China or elsewhere, investor sentiment is badly hit, market operators say. The S&P \f28 \uc2 \f2 BSE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sensex is down 1.2% at 24,640.10, a 52-week low, while the CNX Nifty is down 1.1% at 7,514.40. Metal stocks, that are closely linked to China, are down, namely \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Steel\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500470.BY) which is down 3% and the biggest Sensex loser, followed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500112.BY) down 2.4% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharat Heavy Electricals\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500103.BY) down 2.3%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys (500209.BY) \f28 \uc2 \f2 is least declining stock on the Sensex down 0.1% followed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500325.BY) down 0.3% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hero MotoCorp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500182.BY) down 0.7%. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0402 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A countercyclical buffer recently introduced by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  provides it with a tool to persuade banks to conserve capital and slow credit growth that could help the country during its current slowing cycle, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. "To the extent that the increase in the capital buffer prompts banks to conserve capital and slow their balance sheet growth, it would benefit their credit quality," the report said. The rule took effect at the start of the month as part of efforts to fully adopt the Basel III regulations that determine banks capital adequacy norms. The countercyclical buffer requirement was initially set at 0% of banks' risk-weighted assets, which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said was likely due to a decline in credit growth in Indonesia and a subdued outlook for economic growth. (sara.schonhardt@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0357 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Vietnam is seeking to boost its stock market, including by attracting more foreign investment, Finance Minister Dinh Tien Dung said. Dung said his ministry is working on ways to boost the implementation of a government decree to remove the limit on foreign ownership of locally listed companies. He said Vietnam will also seek to improve the local stock market's credit rating and cut down on administrative procedures to facilitate the participation of foreign investors in the market. Dung said that Vietnam's stock market grew 6.1% last year, with the total market capitalization equaling 57% of the GDP at the end of 2015. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0353 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The liquidity in the offshore yuan market is drying up, squeezing short-term interbank borrowing rates to extreme levels. On Monday morning, the overnight rate that banks in Hong Kong charge each other to borrow yuan soared from 4% Friday to 13.4% (annualized), an all-time high since the Treasury Markets Association started publishing this benchmark rate in 2013. The one-week (annualized) rate surged to 11.23% from 7.05% Friday. It comes after Chinese banks, proxy for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market and bought up the yuan last week. "As these banks are holding the yuan instead of releasing it to the market, liquidity has dried up," says a senior trader at a major local bank. "A lot of channels bringing money from onshore to offshore market have been blocked, which also contributes to the shortage of yuan in Hong Kong," said Tommy Ong, head of Wealth Management Solutions at DBS in Hong Kong. This effectively increased the cost for speculators to borrow and short the yuan, traders say. The spot CNH, or offshore yuan, has become quieter in transaction and stabilized in value. The USD/CNH stands up 6.6727 versus 6.6820 late Friday. (fiona.law@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0333 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Lower crude oil prices will allow Vietnam to continue to cut its input costs to make Vietnamese exports more competitive, boosting economic growth, Minister of Finance Dinh Tien Dung said. Dung said faster economic growth will create more budget revenue, compensating for a decline in revenue from crude oil exports. He said Vietnam is prepared for the scenario where crude oil prices stay as low as $30 per barrel for this year. He said Vietnam will pursue a market-based price for transport fuels. Last year, Vietnam cut transport fuel prices by 12%-30% for different types of products. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "China's economy is beset with a host of problems, but inflation isn't one. Consumer price inflation remains high enough to keep concerns about deflation at bay but low enough to give policymakers plenty of room to loosen further," says Williams. "China Has Problems, but Inflation Isn't One of Them -- Market Talk," at 0219 GMT, misquoted Capital Economics economist Mark Williams.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0322 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Australia's unemployment rate might have further to fall based on current indicators of hiring and job creation, says ANZ chief economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warren Hogan\f28 \uc2 \f2 . He made the comment while pointing to a solid 0.8% trend growth in job advertising in December from November. "The positive job ads trend suggests that the jobless rate should remain below 6% in coming months and could even improve a little further, he added. Official data has shown 130,000 new jobs added over the last two months, with unemployment at an 18 month low of 5.8%. If ANZ is right, ongoing signs of improvement in the job market will go a long way to keeping the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  sidelined. It has remained chilled out since May, keeping the cash rate at 2.0%. It also notes the Australian dollar is knocking on the door of its lowest levels since October 2009. The hurdle to cut rates further might be more than just another soft quarterly inflation read. Fourth quarter CPI data is due January 27. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0319 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mogujie.com\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of China's biggest fashion-focused e-commerce services, said it has agreed to take over its competitor to form a new company that could be valued at nearly $3 billion, in the latest of a series of mergers and acquisitions in China's technology startup sector. The new company that brings together \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mogujie\f28 \uc2 \f2  and rival Meilishuo.com, which is backed by social network giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tencent Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0700.HK), will seek to raise fresh funds after completing the deal, Mogujie Chief Executive Chen Qi said in a letter to employees that was reviewed by The Wall Street Journal. Chen said in the letter that he would become the CEO of the new company. Tencent plans to increase its stake in the new company, a person familiar with the matter said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mogujie\f28 \uc2 \f2 's deal with Meilishuo continues the streak of high-profile M&A deals among Chinese startups. As venture capitalists and other investors become more cautious about putting high price tags on companies that are burning through cash to compete with rivals, startups in China are under pressure to consider teaming up with rivals. (juro.osawa@wsj.com; @JuroOsawa) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0312 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] North Korea's sudden collapse would be a bigger threat to South Korea than an inter-Korean military conflict, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It forms this view even as risk of conflict grows following Pyongyang's fourth atomic bomb test last week. "A regime collapse in North Korea would likely lead to a disorderly reunification on the peninsula, weighing on South Korea's creditworthiness," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in a note. Such a development would generate "acute financial strain" for South Korea. Parliament in Seoul estimates such a disorderly reunification would cost South Korea an annual average of 3.9% of gross domestic product for 45 years and also push Seoul's national debt up to 134% of GDP by 2040 versus 85% if the two Koreas were to remain divided. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the status quo will likely prevail in the region because it expects the U.S. and China to contain the risk of an inter-Korean armed conflict. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10 Jan 2016 23:39 ET \par Hong Kong Stocks--Financials, Property, -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese energy consumption last October and November grew at its slowest pace since the financial crisis. "China Electricity Consumption Lowest Since Financial Crisis -- Market Talk," at 0250 GMT, incorrectly said in the headline that electricity consumption had grown at its slowest pace since the financial crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 10, 2016 23:39 ET (04:39 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160111ec1b000ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
