\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -China gives Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  temporary remedy; weekly losses seen amid pessimism\b0\par\par\uc2 847 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2016\par 07:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixes midpoint higher; yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted\par     * Little conviction on further stabilisation yet\par     * Yuan to see worst week since Aug devaluation\par     * Won leads weekly Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 8 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Friday rebounded as China tried to calm financial markets again,\par while regional units were set to suffer weekly losses on\par uncertainties over Beijing's stance on the renminbi's weakness.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its daily yuan guidance rate\par  firmer, for the first time in nine sessions, helping\par onshore renminbi open sharply higher. That\par supported other emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Malaysian\par ringgit and the South Korean won.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par through state-run lenders to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was on Thursday suspected of bolstering\par offshore yuan after it hit a record low of 6.7600 per\par dollar. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator has ordered banks in some of the\par country's major import and export centres to limit purchases of\par dollars this month, three people with direct knowledge said on\par Friday, in the latest attempt to stem capital outflows.\par  \par     China's major stock indexes rose after Beijing ditched a\par circuit breaker mechanism that halted trading twice this week\par and had been blamed for making market sell-offs worse.\par  \par     "This is only a lull," said Emmanuel Ng, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , referring to a stronger yuan midpoint\par fixing on Friday.\par     "We expect a resumption of upside surprises in the USD/CNY\par midpoints if broad dollar strength regains traction and data\par points more economic slowdown," Ng said.\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to weaken as they react\par more significantly to yuan, he added.\par     Bearish bets on the renminbi hit a near six-year high,\par denting sentiment towards most other regional units, a Reuters\par poll of fund managers, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders and analysts showed on\par Thursday. \par     \par     DANCING WITH YUAN\par     Onshore yuan on Friday initially rose as much as 0.4\par percent, helping its regional peers rebound.\par     But the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gave up most of the gains, cutting\par rises in other emerging Asian units. The Singapore dollar\par  turned weaker.\par     The renminbi has slid 1.4 percent against the dollar so far\par this week, which would be its largest weekly loss since\par mid-August in 2015 when China surprisingly devalued the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     On Thursday, China allowed the biggest fall in the yuan in\par five months, pressurising other emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid\par fears that the move would trigger competitive devaluation.\par     The won was the worst-performing regional unit with a 2.1\par percent slide as North Korea's nuclear test on Wednesday boosted\par geopolitical tensions in the peninsula. In retaliation, South\par Korea unleashed a high-decibel propaganda barrage across its\par border with the North. \par     The South Korean unit is seen weakening further, not because\par of the tensions, but because of a slowing China's economy and\par uncertainty over the yuan, traders said.\par     "We need to open the door for the yuan's further weakness on\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's softer fixing again. That will put more pressure on the\par won, causing more selling from offshore names," said a foreign\par bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader in Seoul.\par     The trader said offshore funds, especially macro accounts,\par sold the won and some long-term foreign investors unloaded the\par unit around 1,200 per dollar.\par     The ringgit has fallen 2.0 percent so far this week as\par sliding crude prices added to concerns over Malaysia's falling\par oil and gas revenues. The country's exports in November rose\par less than expected. \par     Singapore's dollar has lost 1.1 percent throughout this\par week, while the Indian rupee has slumped 0.8 percent.\par     The Taiwan dollar has fallen 0.7 percent for the\par week.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0605 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.26         117.68       -0.49\par   Sing dlr        1.4341         1.4328  