\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan Nearly Flat as  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Stocks Rise on Likely  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2016\par 03:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0237 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The yuan is nearly flat in both the onshore and offshore markets, matching the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's marginal strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Friday benchmark to the U.S. dollar. It is unclear if the authorities are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan stable, though it is a possibility due to the strong likelihood that the government has been employing a heavy hand in the stock market today. Shanghai's stock market opened Friday 2.2% up, then fell as low as 2.2%, before rebounding sharply to its current 1.5% gain. Speculation is rife that the so-called national team has been activated to buy stocks, after Thursday's scrapping of the circuit-breaker rule--possibly due to feedback triggered panic selling. USD/CNY is now 6.5887 from its last close of 6.5929. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 07, 2016 21:37 ET (02:37 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160108ec1800089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
