\par\par \b \uc2 China Stocks Selling Makes NZ Traders Lactose Intolerant -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2016\par 05:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0458 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] New Zealand shares fell on Thursday amid growing concerns about China's economy. The benchmark NZX-50 index lost 0.78%, or 49 points, to 6213.39 on Thursday. Trading on China's stock market was halted after just half an hour on Thursday, after tumbling more than 7%. It's the second time the Chinese share market has closed early this week, and came after \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Thursday. Worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy weighed on New Zealand dairy stocks, with \uc2 The a2 Milk Company\uc2  (ATM.NZ) , Fonterra Shareholders' Fund (FSF.NZ) and Synlait (SML.NZ) all falling. \uc2 The a2 Milk Company\uc2 , which has enjoyed a stellar run lately largely due to strong demand from Chinese consumers, fell 5.34% to NZ$1.74. Fonterra Shareholders' Fund fell 0.65% to NZ$6.07 and Synlait, which sits outside the top 50 index, was down 0.67% to NZ$2.98. (kate.geenty@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 06, 2016 23:58 ET (04:58 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160107ec17000fu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
