\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: Stocks Hit by North Korea, China, Oil\b0\par\par\uc2 1,331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2016\par 12:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Markets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concerns over China, news of a possible nuclear test in North Korea and a steep fall in oil prices combined to send European stocks lower on Wednesday, extending the shaky start to this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 was down 1.2% late morning, led lower by the resources sector as Brent crude fell to an 11-year low and the price of copper declined.\par \par \uc2 Investors shed risky assets and bought into haven investments, spooked by lackluster Chinese services data released on Wednesday. Those concerns were a large factor in oil's decline, as mounting concerns over China's economy spread across markets.\par \par \uc2 "The slowdown in China and its effect more broadly on emerging markets will still be a major theme in the global equity market this year," said David Lafferty, chief market strategist at Natixis Global Asset Management\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index ended up 2.3% Wednesday, but its near 7% plunge at the start of the week has left investors on edge.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to soothe fears and prop up the country's economy.\par \par \uc2 For European equities "China is the only story," said Tristan Abet, investment strategist at Louis Capital Markets. "If you're a bear on China and the yuan, you can't be bullish on Europe," he said.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices fell to an 11-year low, under pressure from a strong dollar and the weak Chinese data, as crude continues to suffer from a persistent supply glut.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also positioning ahead of key U.S. supply data due later in the day. U.S. crude inventories are hovering near high levels not seen in decades and production has been resilient despite the low prices. This adds to the global oversupply of crude that has been battering prices since the summer of 2014.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude, the global oil benchmark, fell 2% to $35.70 a barrel on London's \uc2 ICE\uc2  Futures exchange. On the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 , West Texas Intermediate futures were trading down 2.75% at $35.00 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Gold was up 0.3% at $1,081.20 a troy ounce. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par American Markets Outlook: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures pointed to sharp losses at the open.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures for the Dow Jones Industrial Average slid 1% to 16,920, while those for the S&P 500 index dropped 1.1% to 1,990.50. Futures for the Nasdaq 100 index lost 1.1% to 4,435.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dismal start to 2016 appears to have only intensified this Wednesday, with disappointing Chinese services data (sending the yuan to a 5-year low against the dollar even if the Shanghai Composite managed some counter-intuitive growth), a fresh 11-year low for Brent Crude and reports of a fourth nuclear test from North Korea," said Connor Campbell at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Spreadex\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Later in the day, attention turns to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 ADP\f28 \uc2 \f2  private-employment report in the U.S., as well as the minutes from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's December meeting. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Europe, the euro was down 0.1% against the dollar at $1.0732, while the dollar fell 0.5% against the yen at Y118.5430.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen climbed against its rival \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in choppy Asia trade as soured sentiment on worries about China's economy and fresh geopolitical concerns over the Korean Peninsula prompted investors to buy the safety of the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market reaction shows how bad the market sentiment has been," said Minori Uchida, head of Tokyo global markets research at the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The U.S. is heading toward tightening at the time when the global economy still lacks vigor," said Mr. Uchida. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par Top Stories: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil Prices Fall to 11-Year Low\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices slid to an 11-year low under pressure from a strong dollar and weak Chinese data, as crude continues to suffer from a persistent supply glut.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone Growth Accelerated at End of 2015\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area shrugged off the impact of terror attacks on Paris and security concerns elsewhere-with Italy recording its most rapid expansion in almost five years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No Alternative to Stimulus, Says ECB's Chief Economist\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's top economist Peter Praet said there was no alternative to pursuing the current stimulus program, even though it hasn't yet succeeded in boosting low inflation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Analysis: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iran Crisis Puts Pressure on New Saudi Leaders\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia's decision to execute a firebrand Shiite cleric has encapsulated the complicated ways that the kingdom's challenges affect each other-and can set off volatile reactions across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deaths From Starvation Reported in Damascus Suburb\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At least 10 people have died in recent weeks from starvation in a Damascus suburb that has been under siege by the Syrian regime for seven months, residents and activists said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Container Ships Prepare to Steam into Iran\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some of the world's largest container shipping lines are planning to stop in Iran for the first time in years after the lifting of sanctions, marking a key step in the country's return to international markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Still To Come \par GMT                    Exp   Prev \par 1200 US      MBA Weekly Mortgage \par              Applications Survey \par 1315 CAN Dec Monetary Reserves \par 1315 US  Dec ADP National \par              Employment Report \par              Private Sector Jobs, \par              Q/Q% +195000 +217000 \par 1330 US  Nov International Trade \par              in Goods & Services \par              Trade Balance \par              (\f28 \uc2 \f2 USD\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) -44.0B -43.89B \par              Exports (USD)184.06B \par              Exports, M/M%  -1.4% \par              Imports (USD)227.95B \par              Imports, M/M%  -0.6% \par 1330 CAN Nov International \par              merchandise trade \par              Exports, M/M%  -1.8% \par              Imports, M/M%  -0.8% \par              Trade Balance \par              (CAD)        -2.760B \par 1445 US  Dec Services \par              PMI        55.0 56.1 \par 1500 US  Nov Manufacturers' \par              Shipments, \par              Inventories & Orders \par              Total Orders, \par              M/M%     -0.2% +1.5% \par              Ex-Defense, \par              M/M%           +1.5% \par              Ex-Transport, \par              M/M%           +0.2% \par              Durable Goods, \par              M/M%           +3.0% \par 1500 US  Dec Online Help Wanted \par              Index \par 1500 US  Dec ISM Non- \par              Manufacturing Report \par              on