\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Stocks Steady After China Turmoil\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 11:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks steadied Tuesday, but the tepid recovery reflected investors' caution after a sharp selloff that kicked off the year.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average inched up 10 points, or less than 0.1%, to 17159. The S&P 500 gained 0.2%, but the Nasdaq Composite dropped 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 Fears about a slowdown in China appeared to recede Tuesday, but muted gains highlighted investors' low expectations for 2016 after U.S. stock indexes finished their worst year since 2008.\par \par \uc2 "There's been so much pessimism coming into this year," said \uc2 Randy Warren\uc2 , chief investment officer at \uc2 Warren Financial\uc2 . "We have a chance now for the market to make some ground up."\par \par \uc2 Shares of gun makers rose as U.S. President Barack Obama announced tighter gun-control measures, which could encourage consumers to buy before the measures take effect, analysts said. \uc2 Smith & Wesson Holding\uc2  rose 11% after raising its revenue and profit guidanc e late Monday. Rival Sturm, Ruger & Co. added 6.8%.\par \par \uc2 Wal-Mart Stores\uc2 , the Dow's biggest laggard in 2015, rose the most in the index on Tuesday, adding 2.4%.\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  shares fell 2.8%. A person familiar with the matter said the social media company was planning to increase its 140-character limit on tweets to as many as 10,000.\par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 recovered from earlier losses to rise 0.6%. The Shanghai Composite Index fell 0.3% after Chinese officials outlined a raft of measures to stabilize markets. Monday's 7% drop in mainland Chinese shares, sparked by weak manufacturing data, had triggered circuit breakers that shut down the market and sent ripples through bourses world-wide.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average had its greatest opening-day loss since 2008 Monday.\par \par \uc2 The shaky start to 2016 points to what analysts and investors say will be a volatile year in global markets.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly the fear over China hasn't abated," said Ben Kumar, investment manager at Seven Investment Management, which has more than $9 billion in assets under management and administration.\par \par \uc2 Chinese authorities acted on several fronts to calm investors Tuesday. The stock-market regulator said it would release guidelines about large-scale selling of shares ahead of a ban on selling by large stakeholders that is expected to expire on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected 130 billion yuan ($19.9 billion) in short-term funds into the country's financial system, according to a statement from the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Asia, Japan's Nikkei Stock Average fell 0.4%, while Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index dropped 0.65%.\par \par \uc2 Gold rose 0.3% to $1,078.40 a troy ounce after rising sharply on Monday as investors sought safe havens. The yield on the 10-year \uc2 Treasury\uc2  note rose slightly to 2.248%, compared with 2.245% on Monday. Yields fall as prices rise.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro was down 0.7% against the dollar at $1.0750 after eurozone inflation data for December came in unchanged, below expectations for a modest pickup.\par \par \uc2 Write to Leslie Josephs at leslie.josephs@wsj.com and \uc2 Riva Gold\uc2  at riva.gold@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 05, 2016 05:05 ET (10:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec15000xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
