\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 23:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS STEADY AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks steadied Tuesday, but the tepid recovery reflected investors' caution after a sharp selloff that kicked off the year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. CAR SALES SET RECORD IN 2015 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. car sales hit an annual record, clearing a previous peak reached in 2000 as lower gas prices and interest rates spurred consumers to snap up vehicles from dealerships. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACCOUNTING RULE THAT WHIPSAWED BANKS' EARNINGS TO BE SCRAPPED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Accounting Standards Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would change a rule that requires banks to take losses when some of their own debt is considered safe, and to record gains when the debt is considered riskier. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IN TO PROP UP YUAN \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PIONEER NATURAL RESOURCES\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO BOOK $1 BILLION IN WRITE-DOWNS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pioneer Natural Resources Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it would write down the value of its oil-and-gas properties by around a $1 billion, while the oil-and-gas explorer forecast production growth and higher capital spending for 2016. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIRIUS\f28 \uc2 \f2  XM ADDED MORE USERS THAN IT FORECAST FOR 2015 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sirius XM Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . added more subscribers than expected in 2015 but said it sees that growth slowing in 2016. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YUM CHAIRMAN PLANS TO RETIRE IN MAY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yum Brands\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Executive Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 David C. Novak\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to retire in May, following the fast-food company's annual meeting. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SONIC PROFIT RISES 24% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sonic Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s first-quarter profit rose 24% on continued strong sales at the fast-food chain. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. MORGAN\f28 \uc2 \f2  PAYS $48 MILLION TO CLOSE REGULATORY ORDER ON MORTGAGE SERVICING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Office of the Comptroller of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . would pay a $48 million civil penalty to end a regulatory order against the bank related to mortgage-servicing matters. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. SOLDIER KILLED IN AFGHANISTAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One U.S. serviceman was killed and two wounded during a Special Forces \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Afghanistan's Helmand province on Tuesday, a U.S. military spokesman said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Politics and Policy \par OBAMA UNVEILS EXPANDED GUN CONTROL MEASURES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama announced executive moves to expand background checks for gun buyers and tighten rules for people who purchase some of the most dangerous weapons. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Ahead of the Tape \par FED MAY FIND IT TOUGH TO BUCK THE DOLLAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The debate over exchange rates and sluggish manufacturing activity should garner plenty of attention in Wednesday's release of the Fed's meeting minutes. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Markets Main \par UNCERTAINTY OVER STOCK-SELLING BAN CLOUDS CHINA'S MARKETS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese regulators' murky guidance about whether big stakeholders can resume selling stocks is exacerbating an already volatile week of trading for mainland markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Technology \par DRIVERLESS CARS STEAL THE SHOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Autonomous cars are taking over the Consumer Electronics Show with car makers and nascent auto suppliers making announcements about deepening commitments to driverless vehicles. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par U.S. STOCKS STEADY AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks steadied Tuesday, but the tepid recovery reflected investors' caution after a sharp selloff that kicked off the year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. GOVERNMENT\f28 \uc2 \f2  BONDS TAKE BREATHER AFTER PRICE GAIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds took a breather Tuesday following Monday's price rally that was driven by a large decline in global stocks. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR SOARS TO STRONGEST SINCE 2002 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar gained against most major and emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, driving the U.S. unit to the strongest level in more than 13 years. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL SLIDES TO TWO-WEEK LOW ON SIGNS OF WEAK DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices fell to two-week lows after a round of bearish economic data out of the U.S. and China raised questions about demand for crude. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD PRICES EDGE UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices edged up Tuesday as markets stabilized amid Middle East tensions and concerns over Chinese growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 17:50 ET (22:50 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec150047r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
