\par\par \b \uc2 CANADA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  DEBT-C$ weakest in 12 years; oil, China, rate outlook weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 22:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds strategist comment, details; updates prices)\par     * Canadian dollar ends at C$1.3989, or 71.48 U.S. cents\par     * Bond prices higher across maturity curve\par \par     By Alastair Sharp\par     TORONTO, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar hit its\par weakest point against its U.S. counterpart since mid-2003 on\par Tuesday, as oil prices fell and investors fretted about the pace\par of growth in China and awaited word from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  on\par monetary policy divergence.\par     The loonie, as Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is colloquially known, lost\par 16 percent of its value in 2015 as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  twice cut\par rates to offset the negative impact of low prices for oil, a\par major Canadian export. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in contrast, raised rates last\par month for the first time in almost a decade and has signaled\par more hikes to come. \par     The Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governor, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stephen Poloz\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is to\par speak on the topic of "Life After Lift-off" on Thursday, with\par market players bracing for an updated outlook ahead of the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's interest rate announcement and monetary\par policy report on Jan. 20.\par     "He sounded reasonably confident in mid-December and the\par bank has been loathe to change its tune drastically between\par forecast rounds, so it's not a guarantee, but the data has been\par almost uniformly weak," said Mark Chandler, head of Canadian\par fixed income and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     He said a further risk for the loonie is that the Fed raises\par rates more rapidly than currently priced in by the market.\par     Investor relief at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to steady its\par markets quickly evaporated, while oil traders brushed off rising\par tensions between Saudi Arabia and Iran to push oil toward an\par 11-year low.  \par     The Canadian dollar settled at C$1.3989 to the\par greenback, or 71.48 U.S. cents, weaker than Monday's close of  \par C$1.3941, or 71.73 U.S. cents.\par     At one point it touched C$1.4020, its weakest level since\par August 2003. \par     Canadian producer prices unexpectedly fell 0.2 percent in\par November from October, data from Statistics Canada showed. It\par was the fourth consecutive monthly decline. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canadian government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond prices were higher across the\par maturity curve, with the two-year up 4 Canadian cents\par to yield 0.452 percent and the benchmark 10-year \par rising 22.5 Canadian cents to yield 1.374 percent.\par     Canada is scheduled to release trade data for November on\par Wednesday, its December employment report on Friday and a\par business outlook survey next Monday.\par \par  (Additional reporting by Fergal Smith; Editing by Paul Simao\par and Dan Grebler)\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-5T22:49:22.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160105ec1500rcg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
