\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 851 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 19:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS SLIP AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks slipped Tuesday as investors remained cautious on the heels of a sharp selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. CAR SALES POISED FOR BEST YEAR EVER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. new-car sales accelerated through December as auto makers remained poised to report their highest annual sales ever, shattering the record set in 2000. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ACCOUNTING RULE THAT WHIPSAWED BANKS' EARNINGS TO BE SCRAPPED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Accounting Standards Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would change a rule that requires banks to take losses when some of their own debt is considered safe and rising in value, and to record gains when the debt is considered riskier and declining in value. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IN TO PROP UP YUAN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. SPECIAL FORCES MEMBER KILLED IN AFGHANISTAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A U.S. Special Forces member was killed and two others wounded in fighting in Afghanistan's Helmand province on Tuesday, a U.S. military spokesman said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 VOLKSWAGEN\f28 \uc2 \f2  SEEKS EXTRA TIME TO PROVIDE EMISSIONS DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  asked the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  for more time to provide full data on carbon dioxide emissions from its cars, after it failed to meet an end-of-year deadline, two people familiar with the discussions said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ORANGE ENGAGES \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOUYGUES\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN FRENCH TELECOM MERGER TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French telecom operator Orange has entered preliminary talks to buy the telecom assets of construction-to-media conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bouygues\f28 \uc2 \f2  in an attempt to consolidate France's cutthroat broadband and mobile industries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GERMAN JOBLESS AT 24-YEAR LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German unemployment in 2015 hit its lowest level in almost a quarter of a century, official data showed on Tuesday, but a record influx of migrants will soon start reversing the downward trend. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROZONE INFLATION REMAINS STUBBORNLY LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in the eurozone rose at an unchanged and sluggish pace in December, a fresh sign that it is proving more difficult for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost inflation than policy makers had expected. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SPIRIT AIRLINES NAMES INDUSTRY VETERAN FORNARO AS NEW CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spirit Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  appointed airline-industry veteran and board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert L. Fornaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  as its new chief executive. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LONDON HEDGE FUND NEVSKY CAPITAL TO SHUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 London hedge-fund firm Nevsky Capital plans to shut down and return cash to investors, said 'unsuited' to market dominated by computer-driven trades from algorithmic and index funds. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAUDI ARABIA CUTS EUROPEAN OIL PRICES AS MIDDLE EAST TENSIONS GROW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia sharply cut the prices it charges for crude oil in Europe, a move that could undercut Iran as sectarian tensions escalate between the rival Middle Eastern nations. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA ASKS \f28 \uc2 \f2 MICROSOFT\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO EXPLAIN 'MAJOR PROBLEMS' IN PROBE DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese officials have asked \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2  to explain "major problems" in digital data the U.S. company had provided as part of a probe into its sales and marketing practices in the country. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SLIDES ON INDICATIONS OF WEAK DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices are falling after a round of bearish economic data out of the U.S. and China raised questions about demand for crude in an oversupplied market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NYC BUSINESS ACTIVITY IMPROVES IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business activity in New York City rose in December, though hiring in the area remained weak and owners signaled revenue would cool in the coming months as consumers remain cautious. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FAIRCHILD SAYS OFFER FROM CHINESE GROUP COULD BE 'SUPERIOR PROPOSAL' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fairchild Semiconductor International\f28 \uc2 \f2  said an unsolicited offer from a Chinese investor group likely would constitute a "superior proposal," a potential wrench in the chipmaker's pact to sell itself to \f28 \uc2 \f2 ON Semiconductor\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NOMURA SETTLES AMERICAN EXECUTIVE'S LAWSUIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's largest brokerage has settled a wrongful-dismissal suit filed by Seth Friedman, agreeing to pay him $688,000 in compensation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LILLY ISSUES WEAK FINANCIAL OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eli Lilly\f28 \uc2 \f2  issued downbeat profit and revenue guidance for the new year, but shares rose amid optimism for the drugmaker's medicines in development. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA NAMES ZHAO SHUANGLIAN COFCO CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China shuffled the leadership at the top levels of its big state-owned agribusinesses, drawing a new chairman for global food conglomerate Cofco Corp. from the ranks of the country's grain stockpiling agency. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MANNKIND\f28 \uc2 \f2 , SANOFI END DIABETES DRUG DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MannKind\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced the termination of its licensing pact with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sanofi-Aventis\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the U.S. for the development and sale of its inhaled insulin product Afrezza and signaled that it might look to sell the drug. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par Politics and Policy \par OBAMA UNVEILS EXPANDED GUN CONTROL, EXERCISING HIS EXECUTIVE AUTHORITY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama announced executive moves to expand background checks for gun buyers and tighten rules for people who purchase some of the most dangerous weapons. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Markets Main \par UNCERTAINTY OVER STOCK-SELLING BAN CLOUDS CHINA'S MARKETS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese regulators' murky guidance about whether big stakeholders can resume selling stocks is exacerbating an already volatile week of trading for mainland markets. \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 13:00 ET (18:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec15002po\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
