\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 19:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS SLIP AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks slipped Tuesday as investors remained cautious on the heels of a sharp selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. CAR SALES POISED FOR BEST YEAR EVER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. new-car sales accelerated through December as auto makers remained poised to report their highest annual sales ever, shattering the record set in 2000. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACCOUNTING RULE THAT WHIPSAWED BANKS' EARNINGS TO BE SCRAPPED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Accounting Standards Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would change a rule that requires banks to take losses when some of their own debt is considered safe and rising in value, and to record gains when the debt is considered riskier and declining in value. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IN TO PROP UP YUAN \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. SPECIAL FORCES MEMBER KILLED IN AFGHANISTAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A U.S. Special Forces member was killed and two others wounded in fighting in Afghanistan's Helmand province on Tuesday, a U.S. military spokesman said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 VOLKSWAGEN\f28 \uc2 \f2  SEEKS EXTRA TIME TO PROVIDE EMISSIONS DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  asked the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  for more time to provide full data on carbon dioxide emissions from its cars, after it failed to meet an end-of-year deadline, two people familiar with the discussions said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ORANGE ENGAGES \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOUYGUES\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN FRENCH TELECOM MERGER TALKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French telecom operator Orange has entered preliminary talks to buy the telecom assets of construction-to-media conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bouygues\f28 \uc2 \f2  in an attempt to consolidate France's cutthroat broadband and mobile industries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN JOBLESS AT 24-YEAR LOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German unemployment in 2015 hit its lowest level in almost a quarter of a century, official data showed on Tuesday, but a record influx of migrants will soon start reversing the downward trend. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROZONE INFLATION REMAINS STUBBORNLY LOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in the eurozone rose at an unchanged and sluggish pace in December, a fresh sign that it is proving more difficult for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost inflation than policy makers had expected. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPIRIT AIRLINES NAMES INDUSTRY VETERAN FORNARO AS NEW CEO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spirit Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  appointed airline-industry veteran and board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert L. Fornaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  as its new chief executive. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Politics and Policy \par OBAMA UNVEILS EXPANDED GUN CONTROL, EXERCISING HIS EXECUTIVE AUTHORITY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama announced executive moves to expand background checks for gun buyers and tighten rules for people who purchase some of the most dangerous weapons. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Markets Main \par UNCERTAINTY OVER STOCK-SELLING BAN CLOUDS CHINA'S MARKETS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese regulators' murky guidance about whether big stakeholders can resume selling stocks is exacerbating an already volatile week of trading for mainland markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Moneybeat Blog \par J.P. MORGAN TO ESCHEW WIRES WHEN IT RELEASES FOURTH-QUARTER RESULTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J. P. Morgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is the latest company going wire-less. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par WHY TOO BIG TO FAIL ISN'T OVER IN EUROPE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A new resolution regime for European banks came into force on Jan. 1, but it doesn't solve all problems just yet. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par U.S. STOCKS SLIP AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks slipped Tuesday as investors remained cautious on the heels of a sharp selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. GOVERNMENT\f28 \uc2 \f2  BONDS LITTLE CHANGED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds were little changed Tuesday amid volatile trading in riskier markets following Monday's large decline in global stocks. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DOLLAR SOARS TO STRONGEST SINCE 2002 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar gained against most major and emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, driving the U.S. unit to the strongest level in more than 13 years. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OIL SLIDES ON INDICATIONS OF WEAK DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices are falling after a round of bearish economic data out of the U.S. and China raised questions about demand for crude in an oversupplied market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOLD PRICE RISES AMID CHINA, MIDDLE EAST WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices held gains Tuesday as markets stabilized despite Middle East tensions and concerns over Chinese growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 13:00 ET (18:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec15002nf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
