\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par STOCKS STABILIZE AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks steadied Tuesday after a sharp selloff on the first trading day of the year, but investors remained cautious following turmoil in Chinese markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. CAR SALES POISED FOR BEST YEAR EVER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fiat Chrysler Automobiles\f28 \uc2 \f2  posted a 12.6% gain in December U.S. sales, as auto makers remained poised to report their highest annual sales ever, shattering the record set in 2000. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IN TO PROP UP YUAN \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINRA TO EXAMINE BROKERAGE FIRM CULTURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The culture at brokerages and financial advisory firms is getting a closer look from Wall Street's self-regulator this year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ORANGE ENGAGES \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOUYGUES\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN FRENCH TELECOM MERGER TALKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French telecom operator Orange has entered preliminary talks to buy the telecom assets of construction-to-media conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bouygues\f28 \uc2 \f2  in an attempt to consolidate France's cutthroat broadband and mobile industries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN JOBLESS AT 23-YEAR LOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German unemployment in 2015 hit its lowest level in almost a quarter of a century, official data showed on Tuesday, but a record influx of migrants will soon start reversing the downward trend. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROZONE INFLATION REMAINS STUBBORNLY LOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in the eurozone rose at an unchanged and sluggish pace in December, a fresh sign that it is proving more difficult for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost inflation than policy makers had expected. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPIRIT AIRLINES NAMES INDUSTRY VETERAN FORNARO AS NEW CEO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spirit Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  appointed airline-industry veteran and board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert L. Fornaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  as its new chief executive. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OBAMA TO EXPAND BACKGROUND CHECKS FOR GUN PURCHASES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama is expected to announce a package of executive moves on guns on Tuesday that would expand background checks and tighten rules for individuals who buy some of the most dangerous weapons. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ASKS \f28 \uc2 \f2 MICROSOFT\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO EXPLAIN 'MAJOR PROBLEMS' IN PROBE DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese officials have asked \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2  to explain "major problems" in digital data the U.S. company had provided as part of a probe into its sales and marketing practices in the country. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Technology \par HOME GADGETS STILL A HARD SELL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cascade of gadgets for a smart home, which is due to accelerate at this week's Consumer Electronics show, seems to be running well ahead of consumer desires. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Markets Main \par BEIJING MUDDLES MARKETS WITH MIXED SIGNALS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After spooking global investors by weakening the yuan to an important psychological level and damping hopes for aggressive measures to spur growth, Beijing policy makers Tuesday sought to calm them by injecting nearly $20 billion into the financial system. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Washwire Blog \par CAPITAL JOURNAL DAYBREAK: POLL POINTS TO UPSIDE FOR TED CRUZ, MARCO RUBIO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Complete coverage of election 2016 and more of the biggest news stories and exclusive features from Washington. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  FACES RENEWED PRESSURE ON INFLATION IN 2016 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone inflation averaged zero in 2015. If price pressures remain weak, markets won't wait long before looking for more \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  action. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par STOCKS STABILIZE AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks steadied Tuesday after a sharp selloff on the first trading day of the year, but investors remained cautious following turmoil in Chinese markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TREASURYS SLIGHTLY HIGHER AMID RISK WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys edged up, reflecting some safe-haven demand as investors keep a cautious eye on riskier markets after yesterday's selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR ENDS LOWER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar weakened slightly against the buck, in another wobbly day for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as continued fears over China add to market volatility. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BEARISH U.S., CHINA DATA PUSH OIL DOWNWARD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weaker-than-expected Chinese manufacturing data and U.S. factory orders fueled worries about demand that pushed crude prices lower, despite rising tensions in the Middle East. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOLD PRICE RISES AMID CHINA, MIDDLE EAST WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices rose Tuesday as instability in the Middle East and concerns over Chinese growth fueled further safe haven buying.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 10:00 ET (15:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec150021p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
