\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 822 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par STOCKS STABILIZE AFTER CHINA TURMOIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks steadied Tuesday after a sharp selloff on the first trading day of the year, but investors remained cautious following turmoil in Chinese markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. CAR SALES POISED FOR BEST YEAR EVER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fiat Chrysler Automobiles\f28 \uc2 \f2  posted a 12.6% gain in December U.S. sales, as auto makers remained poised to report their highest annual sales ever, shattering the record set in 2000. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IN TO PROP UP YUAN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FINRA TO EXAMINE BROKERAGE FIRM CULTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The culture at brokerages and financial advisory firms is getting a closer look from Wall Street's self-regulator this year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ORANGE ENGAGES \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOUYGUES\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN FRENCH TELECOM MERGER TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French telecom operator Orange has entered preliminary talks to buy the telecom assets of construction-to-media conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bouygues\f28 \uc2 \f2  in an attempt to consolidate France's cutthroat broadband and mobile industries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GERMAN JOBLESS AT 23-YEAR LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German unemployment in 2015 hit its lowest level in almost a quarter of a century, official data showed on Tuesday, but a record influx of migrants will soon start reversing the downward trend. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROZONE INFLATION REMAINS STUBBORNLY LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in the eurozone rose at an unchanged and sluggish pace in December, a fresh sign that it is proving more difficult for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost inflation than policy makers had expected. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SPIRIT AIRLINES NAMES INDUSTRY VETERAN FORNARO AS NEW CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spirit Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  appointed airline-industry veteran and board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert L. Fornaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  as its new chief executive. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OBAMA TO EXPAND BACKGROUND CHECKS FOR GUN PURCHASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama is expected to announce a package of executive moves on guns on Tuesday that would expand background checks and tighten rules for individuals who buy some of the most dangerous weapons. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA ASKS \f28 \uc2 \f2 MICROSOFT\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO EXPLAIN 'MAJOR PROBLEMS' IN PROBE DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese officials have asked \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2  to explain "major problems" in digital data the U.S. company had provided as part of a probe into its sales and marketing practices in the country. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BEARISH U.S., CHINA DATA PUSH OIL DOWNWARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weaker-than-expected Chinese manufacturing data and U.S. factory orders fueled worries about demand that pushed crude prices lower, despite rising tensions in the Middle East. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FAIRCHILD SAYS OFFER FROM CHINESE GROUP COULD BE 'SUPERIOR PROPOSAL' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fairchild Semiconductor International\f28 \uc2 \f2  said an unsolicited offer from a Chinese investor group likely would constitute a "superior proposal," a potential wrench in the chipmaker's pact to sell itself to \f28 \uc2 \f2 ON Semiconductor\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NOMURA SETTLES AMERICAN EXECUTIVE'S LAWSUIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's largest brokerage has settled a wrongful-dismissal suit filed by Seth Friedman, agreeing to pay him $688,000 in compensation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ISLAMIC STATE RESUMES ATTACK ON LIBYAN OIL PORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Islamic State\f28 \uc2 \f2  fighters resumed attacks on a key oil terminal in eastern Libya, setting a second tank on fire, a Libyan oil official said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ELI LILLY\f28 \uc2 \f2  ISSUES DISAPPOINTING 2016 OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eli Lilly\f28 \uc2 \f2  issued downbeat profit and revenue guidance for the newly started year, as the drugmaker works to launch multiple new medicines. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA NAMES ZHAO SHUANGLIAN COFCO CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China shuffled the leadership at the top levels of its big state-owned agribusinesses, drawing a new chairman for global food conglomerate Cofco Corp. from the ranks of the country's grain stockpiling agency. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. SUES \f28 \uc2 \f2 VOLKSWAGEN\f28 \uc2 \f2  OVER EMISSIONS SCANDAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Department of Justice\f28 \uc2 \f2  sued \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , seeking billions of dollars in penalties over its alleged cheating on emissions tests, deepening woes for the embattled German auto maker. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KUWAIT RECALLS AMBASSADOR TO IRAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kuwait recalled its ambassador to Iran on Tuesday, becoming the latest Sunni Muslim ally of Saudi Arabia to cut or downgrade ties with Tehran amid a rising, sectarian-fueled crisis in the Middle East \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HOME RETAIL GROUP\f28 \uc2 \f2  REJECTS SAINSBURY BID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. grocer J Sainsbury made a cash-and-share approach to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Home Retail Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  that was rejected by the owner of the Argos and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Homebase\f28 \uc2 \f2  brands. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KKR RETAIL CHAIN MILLS FLEET FARM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Private-equity firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 KKR\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it was buying midwest retail chain Mills Fleet Farm for an undisclosed price. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par Technology \par HOME GADGETS STILL A HARD SELL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cascade of gadgets for a smart home, which is due to accelerate at this week's Consumer Electronics show, seems to be running well ahead of consumer desires. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Markets Main \par BEIJING MUDDLES MARKETS WITH MIXED SIGNALS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After spooking global investors by weakening the yuan to an important psychological level and damping hopes for aggressive measures to spur growth, Beijing policy makers Tuesday sought to calm them by injecting nearly $20 billion into the financial system. \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 10:00 ET (15:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec15001z1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
