\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: Stocks Stabilize After China Moves\b0\par\par\uc2 1,166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 13:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Markets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks stabilized Tuesday after a sharp opening-day selloff as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's markets appeared to steady following state \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index closed down 0.3% after Chinese officials outlined a raft of measures to calm investors' nerves. A 7% drop in mainland Chinese shares in the previous session on Monday had triggered circuit breakers that shut down the market and sent ripples through bourses world-wide.\par \par \uc2 Stocks in Europe were flat in early trade, with the Stoxx Europe 600 index erasing opening gains. The index fell 2.5% on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Chinese authorities acted on several fronts to calm investors Tuesday. The stock market regulator said that it would release guidelines about large-scale selling of shares ahead of a ban on selling by large stakeholders that is expected to expire on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected 130 billion yuan ($19.9 billion) in short-term funds into the country's financial system, according to a statement from the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Mainland Chinese stocks were again volatile on Tuesday, falling as much as 3.2% and rising as much as 1% in early trading.\par \par \uc2 Global crude benchmark Brent was down 0.38% at $37.08 a barrel on London's \uc2 ICE\uc2  Futures Europe. West Texas Intermediate was down 0.11% at $36.72 for February deliveries.\par \par \uc2 "With end-of-year positioning out of the way, a renewed focus on the weak Chinese market should see downward pressure remain on commodity prices," ANZ said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The bearish economic data is overriding concerns that tensions in the Middle East will hit oil supply.\par \par \uc2 Still, most analysts believe that geopolitical risk is rising in the region and can't be discounted as factor that will effect supply.\par \par \uc2 "The rhetoric between Riyadh and Tehran has been stepped up to such an extent that further escalation cannot be ruled out," Carsten Fritsch at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  said. "What is more, there is also a risk of the crisis spilling over to other countries in the region."\par \par \uc2 Traders are also watching the escalating violence in Libya, where two oil terminals were attacked.\par \par \uc2 Gold was up 0.2% at $1,077.40 a troy ounce. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par American Markets Outlook: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures slumped on Tuesday, indicating another day of sharp losses ahead, after a surprise cash injection from \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to calm investors' nerves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures for the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 0.7%, to 16,958, while those for the S&P 500 index dropped 0.8% to 1,993.75. Futures for the Nasdaq 100 index fell 0.7% to 4,471.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Investors are bracing themselves for more wild swings given the uncertain global outlook for economic growth and interest rates," said David Papier at ETX Capital, in a note. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was down 0.3% against the dollar at $1.0794 Tuesday in Europe, while the dollar was down 0.1% against the yen at Y119.2660.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, two people familiar with the matter said, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  used some of the nation's biggest state-run banks as agent entities to buy the yuan and sell U.S. dollars, helping the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reverse its deep losses from Monday, the people, who declined to be named, told The Wall Street Journal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One dollar was trading at 6.5199 yuan, down from 6.5338 yuan at Monday's close. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par Top Stories: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone Inflation Remains Stubbornly Low\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in the eurozone rose at an unchanged and sluggish pace in December, a fresh sign that it is proving more difficult for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost inflation than policy makers had expected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Orange Engages \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bouygues\f28 \uc2 \f2  in French Telecom Merger Talks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French telecom operator Orange has started preliminary talks to buy the telecom assets of construction-to-media conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bouygues\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the latest move in the consolidation of France's broadband and mobile sectors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Sues \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  Over Emissions Scandal\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Department of Justice\f28 \uc2 \f2  sued \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , seeking billions of dollars in penalties over its alleged cheating on emissions tests, deepening woes for the embattled German auto maker. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Analysis: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iran, Saudi Arabia Tension Presents Test for \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The diplomatic crisis between Saudi Arabia and Iran presents a new test for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a particularly challenging time for the oil-producing cartel. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ============================ \par Still To Come \par GMT                    Exp   Prev \par 1245 US      The Retail Economist \par              \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  Weekly \par              Chain Store Sales \par              W/W%           -1.6% \par              M/M%           +1.3% \par 1330 CAN Nov Industrial Prices, \par              M/M%           -0.5% \par              Raw Material Prices, \par              M/M%           +0.4% \par 1355 US      Johnson Redbook \par              Retail Sales Index \par              M/M%           -0.5% \par              Y/Y%           +2.0% \par              Latest Wk,Y/Y% +2.5% \par 1445 US  Dec ISM-NY Business \par              Index           60.7 \par 2100 US  Dec Domestic Auto \par              Industry \par              Sales   17.9M 18.19M \par 2130 US      API Weekly \par              Statistical Bulletin \par              Crude          +2.9M \par              Gasoline       +0.5M \par              Distillate   +2.081M \par ============================ \par  \par Global News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Injects $20 Billion to Calm Nervous Investors\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  injected 130 billion yuan ($19.9 billion) in short-term funds into the country's financial system, according to a statement, in an effort to help calm jittery investors after Monday's sharp stock selloff.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Steps In to Prop Up Yuan\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 White House Aims For Neutral Posture in Saudi-Iran Rift\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration strove to appear neutral Monday amid open confrontation between its ally Saudi Arabia and its frequent nemesis Iran, a strategy that risked anger from Riyadh. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Other News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kuwait Recalls Ambassador to Iran\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kuwait recalled its ambassador to Iran on Tuesday, becoming the latest Sunni Muslim ally of Saudi Arabia to cut or downgrade ties with Tehran amid a rising sectarian standoff in the Middle East.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden, Denmark Step Up Border Controls\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden began enforcing tighter border controls in an attempt to reduce the influx of asylum seekers, transforming a Danish railway station into a new epicenter of Europe's migrant crisis and prompting Denmark to adopt similar policies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 High-Speed Trader Plans Thousand-Foot-Plus Tower in Rural England\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The thousand-foot-plus structure is planned for near the Kentish seaside and is intended to beam microwaves across the English Channel for high-frequency trading firms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to tanya.ashreena@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 07:11 ET (12:11