\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Injects $20 Billion to Calm Nervous Investors \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  injected 130 billion yuan ($19.9 billion) in short-term funds into the country's financial system, according to a statement, in an effort to help calm jittery investors after Monday's sharp stock selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Steps In to Prop Up Yuan \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to prop up a weakening yuan, as Beijing adopted a broad suite of measures to stem a selloff in the country's stock market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Recovers in Asia After Selloff \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil prices recouped overnight losses in early Asia trading as tensions in the Middle East remained high, but the move was restrained by worries about expanding world-wide oversupply. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed's Mester Doesn't See Major Risk to U.S. Economy From China Issues \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the Dow Jones Industrial Average posted a sharp decline Monday, Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Loretta Mester\f28 \uc2 \f2  played down the significance of Monday's global stock selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed's Williams Sees Possibility of 3 to 5 Rate Increases This Year \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could see fit to raise interest rates three to five times this year, given economic data remains on the current path, San Francisco Federal Reserve Bank President \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Williams\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a CNBC interview. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par White House Aims For Neutral Posture in Saudi-Iran Rift \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration strove to appear neutral Monday amid open confrontation between its ally Saudi Arabia and its frequent nemesis Iran, a strategy that risked anger from Riyadh. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Sweden, Denmark Step Up Border Controls \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden began enforcing tighter border controls in an attempt to reduce the influx of asylum seekers, transforming a Danish railway station into a new epicenter of Europe's migrant crisis and prompting Denmark to adopt similar policies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par High-Speed Trader Plans Thousand-Foot-Plus Tower in Rural England \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The thousand-foot-plus structure is planned for near the Kentish seaside and is intended to beam microwaves across the English Channel for high-frequency trading firms. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Soros Taps Ted Burdick as Investment Chief \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Five months after \f28 \uc2 \f2 George Soros\f28 \uc2 \f2 's top investor said he was leaving the billionaire's firm, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Soros Fund Management LLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  tapped Ted Burdick as its new chief investment officer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 05, 2016 03:00 ET (08:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160105ec15000rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
