\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks to snap 3-week losing streak; Kazakh tenge tumbles\b0\par\par\uc2 By Claire Milhench   \par \uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2015\par 11:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 18 (Reuters) - Emerging equities slipped on Friday but remained on course to end the week up about 2.4 percent, whilst the Kazakh tenge fell to a new record low, continuing its recent slide on weak oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark emerging equity index fell 0.8 percent as weak fundamentals and low commodity prices reasserted themselves in the wake of Wednesday's 25 basis-point rate hike by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The index was however on course to end a three-week run of losses.\par \par \uc2 "This is the price action we should expect," said Thomas Harr, head of emerging market research at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The Fed move was in line with expectations, which removed some uncertainty. But now we are back focusing on other things in emerging markets like the collapse in oil prices and the negative stories in places like Brazil and South Africa."\par \par \uc2 Chinese mainland shares were up about 0.3 percent but most other Asian stock markets sold off, with Indonesia down 1.9 percent, Hong Kong down 0.5 percent and Korea down 0.13 percent.\par \par \uc2 Russian stocks slid more than 2 percent as oil prices headed for their third weekly loss.\par \par \uc2 A rebound in the Chinese yuan led Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, with the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off new 4-1/2-year lows.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has suffered 10 straight sessions of weakness against the dollar through to Thursday, its longest streak on record.\par \par \uc2 "Over the next one to two months we should see modest pressure on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  led by China," said Harr, citing the risk of further Fed rate hikes and the fact that oil was trading close to its lowest level since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Oil producers' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained under pressure, with the Kazakh tenge, floated earlier this year, falling 3.6 percent to a record low. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  blamed a 15 percent fall in Brent crude prices this month, after \uc2 OPEC\uc2  decided not to cut production.\par \par \uc2 The tenge is down almost 50 percent this year against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly firmed up, however, with the South African rand up 1 percent and the Russian rouble gaining 0.2 percent as the dollar eased against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rouble is on course however to post its fourth straight weekly loss.\par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso fell more than 26 percent on Thursday, its biggest one-day loss in decades, after the government floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Commenting on the float, Simon Quijano-Evans, chief EM strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 , said the short-term implications for inflation were dire.\par \par \uc2 "But the accompanying changes to export taxation will enable numerous sectors in Argentina to start competing worldwide... and eventually helping calm the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  backdrop," he added.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's naira hit new lows in the parallel market on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  advised more restrictions on dollar spending limits on credit cards.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  expressed concern about a debate in the Ukrainian parliament that effectively amounted to a rejection of the government's proposal for a new tax code and budget for 2016. These reforms are key if the country is to keep receiving \uc2 IMF\uc2  bailout funds.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus35t}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  emerging index performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  emerging Europe performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  frontier index performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see ) (Editing by Hugh Lawson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-12-18T11:21:31.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151218ebci00bhy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
