\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yuan rebound lifts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , weekly losses seen\b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2015\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan up on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; down for 7th week\par     * Taiwan dollar up; foreigners sell after rate cut\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SEOUL, Dec 18 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par edged up on Friday thanks to a rebound in China's yuan, although\par regional units were set to suffer weekly losses on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's interest rate hike and a weakening trend in\par the renminbi.\par     The Taiwan dollar rose on exporters' demand for\par settlements but its upside was limited with foreign investors\par selling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par unexpected interest rate cut on Thursday. \par     The yuan turned firmer after hitting a fresh\par 4-1/2-year low as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via state banks to control the pace of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's depreciation. \par     Singapore's dollar rose on the yuan's rebound. The\par city-state's unit closely follows the renminbi as traders and\par analysts believe the Chinese unit to be a part of the\par undisclosed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket used by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  to manage its monetary policy.\par     The Malaysian ringgit advanced with thin liquidity\par as traders covered bearish bets in the worst-performing Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the year ahead of the weekend.\par     Still, gains in emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were seen just as\par profit-taking from the U.S. dollar's strength and unlikely to\par sustain, traders and analysts said. The dollar retreated\par from a two-week high against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "I expect Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to remain under pressure. It is\par not just the Fed hiking rates, but also the decline in the yuan\par and downside growth risks in the region," said Khoon Goh, senior\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for ANZ in Singapore. The Fed on Wednesday raised\par interest rates for the first time in nearly a decade.\par     "Any rebounds in CNY may be brief and unlikely to support\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  much. In fact, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have not\par reacted as much to the yuan depreciation so far, so there may be\par scope for them to play catch up."\par     Risks of capital outflows from emerging Asia grew as\par investors may relocate funds from the region, he said.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are unlikely draw support from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to expand the type of assets it purchases,\par Goh and other analysts said. \par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose 0.5 percent to 32.882 per the U.S.\par dollar as of 0615 GMT from Thursday's close of 33.035. Local\par exporters sold the greenback for settlements.\par     That compared with Thursday's levels around 32.800 before\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened it, traders said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually weakens or cuts gains of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at domestic closing to protect export competitiveness,\par according to traders.\par     The trade-dependent economy along with emerging market peers\par has been suffering from a global economic slowdown, especially\par in China.\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were on the course for weekly\par depreciation.\par     The yuan has slumped 0.4 percent against the dollar so far\par this week, which would be its seventh straight weekly slide, the\par longest weekly losing streak since 2005 when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par revalued. \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to set its daily\par guidance rate at lows in 4-1/2 years.\par     Indonesia's rupiah has lost 0.4 percent so far this\par week on growing corporate dollar demand for year-end payments.\par The Philippine peso has also eased 0.4 percent so far\par this week.\par     The South Korean won ended the week down 0.3 percent as\par foreign investors kept selling Seoul shares. Thailand's\par baht was down 0.2 percent.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0615 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.92         122.55       +0.52\par   Sing dlr        1.4144         1.4184       