\par\par \b \uc2 China's Problem With The Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2015\par 08:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par C1\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 12/15/15) \par    By Lingling Wei \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING -- China's new pledge to unpeg its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the U.S. dollar underscores a difficult fact for Beijing: Actions by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could blunt its efforts to rekindle Chinese growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Fed is widely expected to raise rates this week amid signs of a strengthening U.S. economy. Meanwhile, China's economy is going in the other direction, with Beijing cutting interest rates and making other moves to loosen monetary policy and spur slowing economic growth.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. rate increase could hinder that effort. It likely would make the dollar stronger, forcing \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maintain the peg. That means buying yuan, often from Chinese banks, which effectively takes money out of China's financial system even as Beijing tries to make more money available to its businesses and consumers.\par \par \uc2 Credit already is tight for many Chinese borrowers, especially small and private companies, despite six interest-rate cuts and looser bank-reserve requirements enacted over the past 13 months.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled its hope to break up that dynamic by pegging the yuan to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that includes the dollar, euro, yen and 10 other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , instead of the U.S. dollar alone. That would give the yuan room to fall against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "No longer will \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  undo monetary easing through renminbi purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Uwe Parpart, chief strategist at Reorient Financial Markets, a Hong Kong-based investment bank, using the official name for the yuan. "Reductions in banks' reserve-requirement ratios and interest rates will directly and without obstruction benefit the Chinese economy."\par \par \uc2 But China's intent also has set off selling of the yuan, both within China and in what is known as Hong Kong's offshore market, amid investor expectations that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket means a weaker yuan. The yuan fell to another four-year low, to around 6.4665 per dollar, in early Monday trading on the mainland. It dropped even more in Hong Kong. In late New York trading, the dollar was fetching 6.4569 yuan.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to calm the jittery markets, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  said in an editorial posted on its website on Monday that China's still-high growth rate, ample \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and rising foreign demand for Chinese assets should work together to keep the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a reasonable equilibrium.\par \par \uc2 It is far from clear that China will unpeg its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the dollar -- something it has said it would do in the past only to retreat. Decoupling risks a loss of investor confidence in the yuan's stability, which could lead to more money leaving China, according to Chinese officials and advisers to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Abandoning the peg would be an important step toward achieving monetary-policy independence, but destabilizing capital outflows could hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from doing that," one of the advisers said.\par \par \uc2 In early 2009, four years after it said it would divorce the yuan from the dollar, China hitched the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the greenback again to keep the yuan from falling in the midst of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 China has played down the impact of a Fed rate increase. On Dec. 10, Wang Yungui, the head of the regulation department under \uc2 China's State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a U.S. rate increase would have some impact on China's cross-border capital flows, but it wouldn't be significant.\par \par \uc2 Still, \uc2 PBOC\uc2  officials have hinted in recent months that they were looking for greater flexibility in how they manage the yuan. "Fixing the [yuan's] exchange rate on the dollar would reduce the independence of the monetary policy," Deputy PBOC Gov. \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  said at a news conference in August.\par \par \uc2 China has seen weakened data from trade, industrial production, property investment and other traditional drivers of growth in recent months.\par \par \uc2 The peg has "complicated domestic macroeconomic policy management as economic prospects between the U.S. and China have diverged," said Eswar Prasad, a Cornell University professor and former China head of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some economists say an overvalued yuan relative to its purchasing power has led Chinese companies to cut prices and lower wages to stay competitive. Also, China's exports to Japan and Europe in recent months have declined faster than its sales to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 "The overvaluation of the renminbi is a root cause of China's economic ills these days," said chief economist Lu Zhengwei at China's Industrial Bank Co.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 15, 2015 02:41 ET (07:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020151215ebcf000le\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
