\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  offshore yuan up on suspected c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2015\par 10:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The yuan jumped in late\par offshore trade on Monday on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Chinese\par state banks on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but the onshore spot\par yuan closed weaker.\par     Traders said the onshore spot yuan weakened because the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the yuan's official midpoint at a\par three-month low while refraining from acting to support it in\par intraday trading.\par     The sharp moves come just as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par looks set to approve the inclusion of the yuan in its reserve\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket when it meets on Monday in what is seen as\par symbolic coming of age for the world's second-biggest economy.\par     The offshore yuan opened at 6.4515 per dollar, its\par lowest level in 3 months and priced at a deep discount to the\par onshore rate -  a situation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par resisted in the recent past after an unexpected devaluation in\par August had prompted market speculation of more yuan weakness.\par     It shortly hit an intraday low of 6.4061 before what traders\par suspected was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Chinese state banks that pushed it\par to an intraday high of 6.4230 just ahead of the midday break.\par     It largely traded narrowly afterwards and was moving around\par 6.42 in late trade, strengthening about 0.3 percent from\par Friday's close.\par     The offshore yuan is set to see the biggest daily gain in a\par month if it keeps strengthening by the end of the trade day.\par     The anticipated \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  approval will place the yuan on a par\par with the U.S. dollar, Japanese yen, British pound\par  and euro.\par     In the onshore market, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the\par midpoint rate at 6.3962 per dollar prior to market\par open, 0.07 percent weaker than the previous fix 6.3915.\par     The spot market opened at 6.3970 per dollar and\par closed at 6.3981 , 0.05 percent weaker from the previous close.\par     These movements narrowed the discount of the offshore and\par onshore yuan to 0.50 percent from the onshore spot by 0830 GMT.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.3962   6.3915    -0.07%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3981   6.3952    -0.05%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.03%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -3.04%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.35%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4275    -0.45%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.6225    -3.42%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Lu Jianxin and Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Sam\par Holmes)\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-30T10:22:06.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151130ebbu00a1c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
