\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan firms on stronger midpoint, suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2015\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 20 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan edged up on Friday\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a firmer midpoint and some major\par state-owned banks sold dollars to offset corporate dollar\par demand, traders said.\par     "Some state-owned banks sold dollars in the market," said a\par trader at a Chinese commercial bank in China. "Yet dollar demand\par by companies has persisted as dollar broadly strengthened."\par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been supported by state-owned\par banks' dollar sales on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said,\par since the yuan's surprise devaluation on Aug. 11.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.3780 per dollar prior to market open, 0.02 percent firmer\par than the previous fix 6.3791.  \par     The spot market opened at 6.3780 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3809 by midday, 0.05 percent stronger\par than the previous close.\par     Dollar sales by state banks appeared to temper any impact\par from a Reuters' report that the yuan's weighting in the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 's benchmark \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket may be\par lower than the 14-16 percent range estimated by economists.\par  \par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may also have been buoyed by recent\par statements by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials that they do not expect\par much market disruption from an anticipated rate hike in\par December, in part because it has been so well telegraphed in\par advance. \par     The yuan's value has been under downward pressure of late\par partly in anticipation that the United States would raise\par benchmark interest rates in December, which could strengthen the\par dollar in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par     Offshore yuan was trading 0.43 percent weaker than the\par onshore spot at 6.4083 per dollar. \par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.3780   6.3791    0.02%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3809   6.3840    0.05%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.05%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.77%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.71%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4083    -0.43%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.5925    -3.25%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Jacqueline\par Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-20T05:18:53.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151120ebbk005vf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
