\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China's Oct commercial bank  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  sales fall 82 percent as outflows slow\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2015\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (add details)\par \par \uc2 By Sue-Lin Wong\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Nov 18 (Reuters) - China's commercial banks sold a net $20.1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements in October, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said on Wednesday, falling sharply from September's $109.2 billion amid signs of easing capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 Capital outflows eased in October as the domestic stock market recovered after a crash over the summer, alongside the government's efforts to clamp down on illegal money transfers, although concerns remain over \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to keep the yuan steady after it devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by nearly 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 "This data can be seen as supporting the idea that conditions calmed significantly after big outflows in August and September," said Tim Condon, an economist at ING in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "I credit the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's exchange rate policy."\par \par \uc2 China's surprise devaluation of the yuan on Aug. 11 fueled a wave of capital outflows on fears the economy might be slowing more sharply than thought and on worries of a possible interest rate rise by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In January-October, commercial banks had net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales of $321.6 billion, the regulator said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 OECD\uc2  said recent government measures, including stricter checks on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by firms and individuals and a crackdown on illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, may have curbed capital outflows for now.\par \par \uc2 "Narrowing of the interest differential and slowing growth, however, may lead to further capital outflows and pressure on the exchange rate," it said.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks bought a net $2.02 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed on Sunday, stemming heavy sales in the previous three months that underlined capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 "Ancedotal evidence suggests that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has borrowed sizable U.S. dollars from the forward market to defend the CNY," Kevin Lai and Junjie Tang from Daiwa Capital Markets wrote in a research report on November 11, adding it would be difficult to determine money outflows by tracking changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sue-Lin Wong; Editing by Kevin Yao and Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-18T06:00:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151118ebbi005mw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
