\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls on strong dollar, in line with weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2015\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 18 (Reuters) - China's yuan softened against\par the dollar on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a weaker\par guidance rate, continuing the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakening trend\par in November. \par     Reflecting the gain of the dollar index, which\par climbed to a seven-month peak on Tuesday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par set Wednesday's yuan midpoint rate at 6.3796 per\par dollar prior to market open, 0.09 percent weaker than the\par previous fix 6.3740. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3830 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3848 at midday, 0.1 percent weaker than\par the previous close. The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has overall slowly\par weakened since Nov. 3.\par     "The dollar has strengthened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par late and we saw the yuan depreciate steadily in a short-term,"\par said a trader at a foreign bank in Shanghai. "It might fall as\par low as 6.40 in the next two weeks."\par     China's commercial banks sold a net $20.1 billion of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in October settlements, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator\par said on Wednesday, compared with $109.2 billion in September.\par     Capital outflows eased in October as the domestic stock\par market recovered after a crash over the summer although concerns\par remain over China's economic slowdown. \par     The yuan's real effective exchange rate (REER), or the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value against the trade-weighted basket after\par adjustments based on inflation, declined for the third month of\par 0.81 percent in October, the BIS data issued on Tuesday showed.\par     The offshore yuan was choppy in early trade, partly\par due to investors' nervousness after Monday's suspected offshore\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     It was trading 0.50 percent weaker than the onshore spot at\par 6.4166 per dollar by midday. \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.3796   6.3740    -0.09%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3848   6.3786    -0.10%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.08%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.83%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.63%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4166    -0.50%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.598     -3.31%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                