\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan dips on uncertainty over suspected offshore \uc2 PBOC \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2015\par 05:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 17 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan weakened on\par Tuesday as some investors sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid uncertainty\par over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in the\par past 24 hours.\par     Some traders suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought the yuan in\par the offshore market on Monday afternoon, causing the offshore\par spot to converge with the onshore market price. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.374 per dollar prior to market open, firmer than the\par previous fix 6.375. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3750 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3751 at midday, 27 pips away from the\par previous. \par     "Some investors sold the yuan maybe to avoid risk," said an\par onshore trader at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     "After the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to bolster the offshore\par yuan, we have no idea whether it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the onshore\par market next."\par     The offshore yuan strengthened over 300 basis\par points on Monday, in what traders said was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par Chinese state banks, probably on behalf of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Concerns the yuan could remain pressured following China's\par unexpected devaluation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in August had caused the\par offshore yuan to trade at a discount to the onshore yuan. \par     Traders believe the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is keen to narrow the gap between\par the onshore and offshore price as it seeks to bolster confidence\par in the yuan ahead of its expected inclusion in the \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (\f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\par     The head of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Friday that its Executive Board\par would meet on Nov. 30 to consider whether to include the Chinese\par yuan into its Special Drawing Rights (SDR) basket..\par     On Tuesday, the offshore yuan was trading 0.40 percent\par weaker than the onshore spot at 6.4004 per dollar. It was around\par 0.6 percent weaker than the onshore yuan intraday on Monday.\par     In the next year or so, the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to\par remain under downward pressure due to slower economic growth. A\par run of recent data has failed to dispel concerns the world's\par second-biggest economy is in need of further stimulus to restore\par momentum.\par \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.374    6.375     0.02%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3751   6.3724    -0.04%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.02%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.68%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.83%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4004    -0.40%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.566     -2.92%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     \par \par  \par   \par \par \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Shri\par Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-17T05:39:50.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151117ebbh005sf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
