\par\par \b \uc2 Copper Falls to Lowest Price Since August\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ese Erheriene   \par \uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2015\par 14:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON--The price of copper fell to its lowest level since August in London on Thursday, as future demand prospects from top consumer China diminished after a series of weaker-than-expected economic data.\par \par \uc2 The London Metal Exchange's three-month copper contract was down 1.4% at $4,872 a metric ton in midmorning European trade, a three-month low.\par \par \uc2 The metal has hovered at near six-year lows in recent weeks, as China's economy has struggled to continue growing at 7%, despite a series of economic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  consumes more than 40% of global copper production.\par \par \uc2 According to data from the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  on Thursday, Chinese lending dropped sharply in October after hitting a September high, showing the limits of Beijing's efforts to use credit to help kick-start faltering growth. On Wednesday, \uc2 China's National Bureau of Statistics\uc2  reported that a decline in the country's industrial production growth. Earlier in the week saw the release of weak Chinese exports that signaled a deflationary trend, and poorer-than-expected trade data.\par \par \uc2 "Weaker demand prospects due in part to a slowing Chinese economy ... are unnerving investors the most," said Fawad Razaqzada, an analyst at Gain Capital.\par \par \uc2 Supply cuts from major producers have failed to alleviate market fears that copper prices could head lower. Last month, \uc2 Freeport-McMoRan Inc\uc2 . said it would further curtail copper production, including a possible shutdown of its Sierrita mine in Arizona. And in September, \uc2 Glencore PLC\uc2 --the world's largest copper supplier and third-largest copper miner-- said it would shut two large African mines for 18 months, removing 400,000 tons of copper from the market.\par \par \uc2 Going forward, metal prices are likely to be dictated by market sentiment about the potential for a rise in U.S. interest rates by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strongly indicated it will increase rates next month, after keeping them unchanged in October and in September.\par \par \uc2 "We saw markets react quite strongly last week concerning the comments coming out of the Fed," said David Wilson, director of metals research and strategy at Citigroup Inc. "If we have another week of strong employment data that will further reinforce the view that a December hike is coming and on the back of that we might see further dollar strength."\par \par \uc2 Copper is used in everything from kitchenware to construction and is priced in dollars. Should the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keep interest rates unchanged, this would likely pressure the dollar lower. When the greenback weakens, the industrial metal becomes cheaper for those holding stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy, and prices often rise with demand.\par \par \uc2 Among the other base metals, aluminum was down 1% at $1,502.50 a ton, zinc was down 1.4% at $1,601 a ton, nickel was down 1.6% at $9,505 a ton, lead was down 0.3% at $1,614.50 a ton and tin was down 1.2% at $14,645 a ton.\par \par \uc2 Neanda Salvaterra contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ese Erheriene at ese.erheriene@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 12, 2015 08:20 ET (13:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020151112ebbc00247\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
