\par\par \b \uc2 Looming Fed Hike Pressures China  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves, Says SG -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2015\par 05:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0331 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves likely fell at a slower rate in October than previous months, but there's a chance outflows could rise ahead of the looming Fed interest-rate increase, says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in a report. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve numbers will likely reveal a drop $20-$25 billion in October when data are released Saturday, it says. That compares with decreases of $40 billion in September and $110 billion in August, when China used its reserves to stabilize the yuan after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the house adds. A dovish Fed meeting in September that set off a rally in emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "probably helped ease pressure from outflows for \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well and lessened the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  burden on the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it says.\par \par \uc2  "However, we think that the pressure will pick up again soon, since, at its October meeting, the Fed reminded the market not to discount the possibility of a December lift-off."(Dominique.fong@wsj.com; Twitter: @dominiquefong)\par \par \uc2 Editor JSM\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 06-11-15 0420GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020151106ebb60004v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
