\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Solid stocks support Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; won up after S.Korea inflation at 11-month high\b0\par\par\uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2015\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * More S.Korea rate cuts unlikely\par     * Taiwan dollar gains on stock inflows\par     * Rupiah up as Indonesia shares jump\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 3 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose on Tuesday as regional stock markets advanced on hopes that\par the global economy may be slowly pulling out of a soft patch.\par     South Korea's won gained as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par stopped short of signalling additional interest rate cuts after\par inflation in October accelerated to its highest in 11 months.\par   \par     The Taiwan dollar hit a one-week high on stock\par inflows, while the Indonesian rupiah advanced more than\par 1 percent as local equities jumped.\par     MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan\par  broke a five-day losing streak, rising 1.3\par percent, after a survey found global manufacturing growth\par accelerated to a seven-month high in October although the\par expansion remained muted. \par     The Chinese yuan barely moved as state-own banks\par sold dollars to offset companies' strong demand, although that\par was on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . That came as the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 raised the midpoint fixing of the\par yuan by the most in a single day since the landmark revaluation\par in 2005.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilise the\par yuan since its devaluation on Aug. 11, especially ahead of the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 's executive board decision on\par whether to put the yuan on a par with the dollar, yen, euro and\par pound, known as the Special Drawing Rights (SDR) basket.\par  \par     The stabilisation efforts supported other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par as the devaluation has sparked expectations that China's\par neighbours may weaken their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to shore up exports.\par     Still, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be hit hard if Beijing loosens\par its grip on the yuan, analysts said.\par     "The risk of PBOC relinquishing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after positive\par statement from the IMF remains acute in coming weeks," said Andy\par Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par in Singapore.\par     "Into the year-end, USD/Asia either grind higher on a firmer\par USD or spike if PBOC changes track on the exchange rate policy."\par     \par     WON\par     The won gained after data showing South Korea's consumer\par price index rose 0.9 percent in October from a year earlier, the\par fastest rise since November last year, reflecting a further\par recovery in consumption.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  refrained from indicating further rate\par cuts as it keeps wary of household debt level and external\par risks, while it promised to maintain its monetary policy easy.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose 1.0 percent to 32.385 per the U.S.\par dollar, its strongest since Oct 27, in thin trading on demand\par from some foreign financial institutions amid higher local\par stocks.\par     The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also found support from gains in the\par won, traders said.\par     Still, traders stayed cautious ahead of a key U.S. jobs data\par due on Friday.\par     Exporters were on the sidelines as they did not see the\par level of around 32.400 as attractive.\par         \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah advanced nearly 1 percent as Indonesia's stocks\par  rallied 1.6 percent, well outperforming Southeast Asian\par peers.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's non-deliverable forwards rose on\par demand from real money accounts and short-term funds.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,594, stronger than the\par previous 13,682.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0655 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.62         120.77       +0.12\par   Sing dlr        1.3953         1.3972       +0.14\par   Taiwan dlr      32.412         32.721       +0.95\par   Korean won     1130.37        1137.00       +0.59\par   Baht             35.54          35.63       +0.24\par   Peso             46.78          46.85       +0.14\par   Rupiah        13550.00       13665.00       +0.85\par   Rupee            65.45          65.59       +0.21\par   Ringgit         4.2820         4.3020       +0.47\par   Yuan            6.3369         6.3379       +0.02\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  