\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Chinese yuan makes biggest one-day gain vs dollar since 2005\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2015\par 14:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds quote, adds LONDON to dateline)\par \par \uc2 By Lu Jianxin, Pete Sweeney and Jemima Kelly\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/LONDON, Oct 30 (Reuters) - China's yuan made its biggest one-day gain against the dollar in more than 10 years in onshore markets on Friday, as traders speculated that state-owned banks had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.6 percent on the day to hit 6.3171 yuan just before the market closed at 0830 GMT. That would not be an especially eye-catching move for other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but for the yuan, still tightly controlled by Beijing, it was the biggest daily gain since its one-off revaluation in July 2005.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Dominic Bunning in London, the biggest hub for yuan trading outside Asia, said the steps China was taking to liberalise the yuan, also called the renminbi, meant moves of this scale would become more common.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to have to be more prepared for seeing days when the renminbi does trade in this manner," he said. "Daily ranges are going to get bigger and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to move in a more volatile manner."\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) \uc2 was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading to support the yuan in the offshore market on Thursday evening, pushing it up sharply, catching some traders by surprise and forcing them into stop-loss orders on Friday, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "We still saw some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the state-owned banks today, plus a bout of stop-loss trades appearing when the CNH (offshore yuan) firmed to around 6.34 and then kept appreciating," said an offshore trader at an Asian bank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Some traders linked the support for the yuan to the IMF's forthcoming internal debate on whether to include the yuan in the Special Drawing Rights (SDR) basket.\par \par \uc2 "PBOC \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today appeared to be stronger than usual," said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 "It appears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may want the yuan to shows more strength ahead of the IMF's discussion on whether to include the yuan into the SDR basket."\par \par \uc2 The offshore yuan, which trades more freely than its onshore counterpart and can be bought and sold 24 hours a day, also gained in much higher than average volume, though not by as much. By 1210 GMT it was up 0.3 percent at 6.3295 yuan per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the yuan's strength, the PBOC set the official midpoint rate at 6.3495 per dollar prior to the onshore market's open - 0.16 percent firmer than the previous fix at 6.3596.\par \par \uc2 The ruling Communist Party of China on Thursday night reiterated its goal of doubling GDP and incomes between 2010 and 2020. Also, Germany and China announced that they will cooperate to create new yuan-denominated trading platforms on Deutsche Bourse which would boost use of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  globally.\par \par \uc2 HBSC's Bunning also highlighted the fact that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  had refrained from expanding its stimulus programme at a policy meeting on Friday, which could dampen any perception of an Asian "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" of competitive devaluations.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Jamie McGeever in London; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore and Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-30T14:05:08.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151030ebau0084i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
