\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan inches up on suspected c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2015\par 05:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 27 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan firmed against the\par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, underpinned by suspected dollar sales\par by state banks on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     "Some state-owned banks sold dollars after a bout of\par dollar-purchases by companies," said a trader at a foreign bank\par in Shanghai.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to want to keep the yuan stable \par to increase the opportunity that it could be included in the SDR\par (Special Drawing Rights) basket," the trader said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.3494 per dollar prior to market open, 0.09 percent firmer\par than the previous fix 6.3549. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3490 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3513 at midday, 0.03 percent firmer than\par the previous close.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 's executive board is\par scheduled to decide in November whether to put the yuan on the\par lender's benchmark \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket, known as SDR, and a key\par factor will be the yuan's performance against a checklist of\par technical criteria. \par     Including the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the SDR basket would give\par it an official seal of approval, eventually leading to global\par demand worth more than $500 billion in coming years, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par analysts say. \par     The offshore yuan was more volatile and was 0.52\par percent, or 350 pips, weaker than the onshore spot rate at\par 6.3846 per dollar by midday. \par     "The spread between the onshore and offshore yuan is\par expected to be between 200 and 500 pips in the near future,"\par said an offshore trader at an Asian bank in Hong Kong.   \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par         ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.3494   6.3549    0.09%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3513   6.3529    0.03%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.03%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.32%\par  Spot change since 2005                30.31%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.3846    -0.52%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.531     -2.78%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Jacqueline\par Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-27T05:08:04.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151027ebar005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
